WEBVTT

1
00:00:18,291 --> 00:00:21,500
[mysterious music playing]

2
00:00:44,833 --> 00:00:45,958
[man] Neil!

3
00:00:47,083 --> 00:00:48,375
[woman] Neil!

4
00:00:48,958 --> 00:00:52,000
[dogs barking]

5
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:53,375
[man] Neil Spencer!

6
00:00:53,875 --> 00:00:55,583
[woman] Neil Spencer!

7
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:59,000
[man] Neil!

8
00:00:59,833 --> 00:01:01,916
Anything more on the parents?

9
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,041
[man 2] <i>Background checks</i>
<i>dug up nothing new.</i>

10
00:01:04,125 --> 00:01:08,375
<i>Dad's AWOL, mom's in rehab,</i>
<i>grandma's been taking care of the boy.</i>

11
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:09,833
All right.

12
00:01:10,333 --> 00:01:12,458
I want all interviews
with immediate family in the area

13
00:01:12,541 --> 00:01:13,750
complete by the end of the day.

14
00:01:13,833 --> 00:01:15,083
[man 2] <i>Yes, Detective.</i>

15
00:01:16,333 --> 00:01:17,291
[man 1] Neil!

16
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:20,000
-Neil!
-[woman over radio] <i>This is not a race.</i>

17
00:01:20,083 --> 00:01:22,333
<i>Take your time.</i>
<i>We're looking for a missing child.</i>

18
00:01:22,416 --> 00:01:24,000
All right, people.

19
00:01:24,541 --> 00:01:25,458
Listen up!

20
00:01:25,541 --> 00:01:28,708
All right, Neil Spencer was put to bed
around 8:00 p.m. last night.

21
00:01:28,791 --> 00:01:32,791
His grandmother reported him missing
at 10:29 p.m.

22
00:01:32,875 --> 00:01:35,958
Be prepared to call your families
and let them know you won't be home.

23
00:01:36,041 --> 00:01:38,583
[man 3] Detective! We found something.

24
00:01:38,666 --> 00:01:40,833
[tense music playing]

25
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:51,500
[somber piano music playing]

26
00:02:08,833 --> 00:02:10,625
This isn't Neil Spencer.

27
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[music fades]

28
00:02:29,083 --> 00:02:32,083
["Shiny Happy People" by R.E.M.
playing over radio]

29
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:36,666
<i>♪ Meet me in the crowd… </i>♪

30
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:39,583
You know, I'm excited.
It's a fresh start, right?

31
00:02:41,625 --> 00:02:42,625
-Yeah?
-Yeah.

32
00:02:42,708 --> 00:02:46,166
You know, your mom always wanted us
to move back to the town we grew up in.

33
00:02:46,666 --> 00:02:49,791
You know, it's cool. You'll be going
to the same school she did. Right?

34
00:02:49,875 --> 00:02:51,083
-Yeah.
-[dad] Yeah.

35
00:02:52,083 --> 00:02:54,208
Plus, we found a house with a swing.

36
00:02:54,291 --> 00:02:57,541
I mean, it's just like the one
you guys loved at the shore.

37
00:02:57,625 --> 00:02:59,375
You've said.

38
00:02:59,458 --> 00:03:00,958
Like a thousand times.

39
00:03:01,041 --> 00:03:02,625
No, no, no. No, that's incorrect.

40
00:03:02,708 --> 00:03:04,791
I've only said it 936 times.

41
00:03:04,875 --> 00:03:06,833
-[chuckles]
-[dad] So get your facts straight.

42
00:03:11,708 --> 00:03:13,000
I miss her.

43
00:03:15,916 --> 00:03:17,083
Me too, buddy.

44
00:03:19,791 --> 00:03:22,916
Up! Get your legs up.
Get 'em up. Come on. Up, up, up, up, up!

45
00:03:24,208 --> 00:03:27,333
And… we are in Garretton.

46
00:03:27,416 --> 00:03:29,125
<i>♪ Everyone around… </i>♪

47
00:03:29,208 --> 00:03:30,166
We did it.

48
00:03:30,875 --> 00:03:34,791
<i>♪ Love them, love them </i>♪

49
00:03:34,875 --> 00:03:38,375
<i>♪ Put it in your hands </i>♪

50
00:03:38,458 --> 00:03:42,208
<i>♪ Take it, take it… ♪</i>

51
00:03:44,166 --> 00:03:45,166
[radio turns off]

52
00:03:45,250 --> 00:03:47,250
[indistinct chatter in background]

53
00:03:59,208 --> 00:04:00,333
There it is.

54
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:03,125
-Wanna go check it out?
-Yeah.

55
00:04:03,208 --> 00:04:04,083
Go ahead.

56
00:04:05,625 --> 00:04:06,875
-Hey, guys.
-[man 1] What's up?

57
00:04:06,958 --> 00:04:10,041
[man 2] Hey, how you doing?
Uh, where do you want these, sir?

58
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:13,166
[dad] Yeah, you know what?
Those can go in the kitchen. Thank you.

59
00:04:19,416 --> 00:04:22,375
-[kid] Hey, Dad! Look at this!
-Be right there, buddy.

60
00:04:32,083 --> 00:04:34,583
I hope this place is
big enough for you, Jake.

61
00:04:36,500 --> 00:04:38,500
[mysterious music playing]

62
00:04:48,541 --> 00:04:51,625
All right, come on, kiddo.
We got a new house, new stairs.

63
00:04:51,708 --> 00:04:53,250
What did we say we were gonna be?

64
00:04:55,708 --> 00:04:56,833
[whispers] Brave.

65
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:58,458
That's right.

66
00:04:59,083 --> 00:05:01,375
Just like your mom when she was sick.

67
00:05:03,541 --> 00:05:04,375
Come here.

68
00:05:06,125 --> 00:05:09,333
All right. Let's go upstairs.

69
00:05:09,958 --> 00:05:11,083
Yeah.

70
00:05:15,166 --> 00:05:17,125
And…

71
00:05:17,958 --> 00:05:19,083
Go find your room.

72
00:05:49,625 --> 00:05:50,833
What's wrong?

73
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:54,000
Why are you so scared?

74
00:05:57,166 --> 00:05:58,458
It's gonna be fine.

75
00:06:02,583 --> 00:06:05,083
[dad] No, not… No! Wait a second.

76
00:06:05,166 --> 00:06:06,291
You can't take him.

77
00:06:06,375 --> 00:06:07,916
Okay, Saturn's going…

78
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,041
Do-do-do-do-do-do!

79
00:06:10,125 --> 00:06:11,041
…right up to the sun.

80
00:06:11,125 --> 00:06:12,041
Do-do-do-do!

81
00:06:12,125 --> 00:06:13,625
-[Jake] No!
-[dad] Chain reaction.

82
00:06:13,708 --> 00:06:14,541
No!

83
00:06:14,625 --> 00:06:16,333
Oh no!

84
00:06:16,416 --> 00:06:18,416
[excited chatter in background]

85
00:06:19,625 --> 00:06:21,000
All right. Uh…

86
00:06:21,083 --> 00:06:22,666
-Okay. You ready?
-[Jake] Yeah.

87
00:06:22,750 --> 00:06:24,750
Good? It's gonna be great. Okay?

88
00:06:26,041 --> 00:06:29,166
You warm enough?
Yeah? Wanna hang onto that?

89
00:06:29,916 --> 00:06:30,750
You sure?

90
00:06:31,708 --> 00:06:32,833
Yeah?

91
00:06:32,916 --> 00:06:33,958
Okay. All right.

92
00:06:34,041 --> 00:06:35,083
Come here.

93
00:06:36,125 --> 00:06:38,208
All right. Have a good day, okay?

94
00:06:38,291 --> 00:06:40,625
I'm gonna be right here
when school gets out, all right?

95
00:06:41,125 --> 00:06:43,375
-Okay. Okay?
-Hmm.

96
00:06:53,791 --> 00:06:58,625
[thunder rumbling]

97
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:27,208
[slow tapping]

98
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,166
Oh fuck.

99
00:07:41,166 --> 00:07:42,500
Jesus.

100
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:50,541
[rain dripping slowly]

101
00:07:56,458 --> 00:07:58,666
[tapping on keyboard]

102
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:14,416
[unsettling music playing]

103
00:08:18,541 --> 00:08:21,083
<i>If your window's left unlatched</i>

104
00:08:21,916 --> 00:08:24,375
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

105
00:08:24,458 --> 00:08:27,875
[kettle whistling]

106
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:42,083
[unsettling music building]

107
00:09:51,791 --> 00:09:53,791
[somber music playing]

108
00:09:54,583 --> 00:09:56,583
[man whispering on tape]
<i>What kind of fish were they?</i>

109
00:09:57,083 --> 00:09:58,541
[Tony] <i>I don't know.</i>

110
00:09:58,625 --> 00:10:02,041
<i>There was a pink one. And a blue one.</i>

111
00:10:02,958 --> 00:10:04,916
[Whisper Man] <i>Do you think</i>
<i>they'll miss you?</i>

112
00:10:05,708 --> 00:10:07,208
[Tony] <i>My fish?</i>

113
00:10:07,291 --> 00:10:10,541
[Whisper Man] <i>You fed them, right?</i>
<i>Like your daddy fed you.</i>

114
00:10:11,041 --> 00:10:14,291
<i>Do you think they'll miss you</i>
<i>feeding them?</i>

115
00:10:15,625 --> 00:10:18,208
-[Tony mumbles] <i>I don't know.</i>
-[Whisper Man] <i>Speak up, boy.</i>

116
00:10:18,791 --> 00:10:21,041
<i>What if they get hungry</i>
<i>and you're not there?</i>

117
00:10:21,541 --> 00:10:23,500
<i>Do you think they'll eat each other?</i>

118
00:10:24,250 --> 00:10:28,541
<i>When one fish is shitting out the other,</i>
<i>will they be thinking of you?</i>

119
00:10:28,625 --> 00:10:31,250
[unsettling music]

120
00:10:37,458 --> 00:10:38,625
[man] Good.

121
00:10:39,916 --> 00:10:42,416
Good. I think they're going to love this.

122
00:10:47,041 --> 00:10:48,458
That's for later.

123
00:11:21,166 --> 00:11:22,708
[banging on door]

124
00:11:22,791 --> 00:11:25,791
[thunder rumbling, rain pattering]

125
00:11:29,791 --> 00:11:31,166
[woman] Hi, Mr. Willis.

126
00:11:31,666 --> 00:11:34,041
Uh, Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

127
00:11:34,541 --> 00:11:35,500
May I come in?

128
00:11:36,666 --> 00:11:38,416
I'm sorry to interrupt your dinner.

129
00:11:39,041 --> 00:11:42,208
Uh, a boy went missing
in Hillcrest a couple of days ago.

130
00:11:42,291 --> 00:11:43,541
Neil Spencer.

131
00:11:43,625 --> 00:11:46,166
We've cleared locations,
family, and friends.

132
00:11:46,791 --> 00:11:50,541
We found something, and I don't know
if it's a lead or a distraction.

133
00:11:54,583 --> 00:11:56,458
Another body. A boy.

134
00:11:56,541 --> 00:11:58,458
Been out in the woods about a month.

135
00:12:04,666 --> 00:12:06,708
Not every kid
who disappears in North Jersey

136
00:12:06,791 --> 00:12:08,708
is connected to Frank Carter, Detective.

137
00:12:08,791 --> 00:12:10,666
But that's his signature, right?

138
00:12:10,750 --> 00:12:13,291
Well, Frank Carter's doing life
in Rahway now.

139
00:12:14,208 --> 00:12:15,333
That's not what I asked.

140
00:12:17,041 --> 00:12:20,833
I know you need to find him, of course,
but I don't know if I can help you.

141
00:12:20,916 --> 00:12:22,958
[Beck] The other boy who went missing,
Neil Spencer,

142
00:12:23,041 --> 00:12:26,833
told his grandma he heard a strange voice
outside his window

143
00:12:27,666 --> 00:12:28,958
whispering to him.

144
00:12:31,625 --> 00:12:34,291
Well, you know,
kids have active imaginations--

145
00:12:34,375 --> 00:12:36,958
Yes, that's what Carter preyed on.
That's what you said.

146
00:12:37,041 --> 00:12:39,125
I did, but, you know,
I'm not on the job anymore.

147
00:12:39,208 --> 00:12:42,000
It's been a long time.
I'm retired at least 25 years.

148
00:12:42,083 --> 00:12:44,291
I just, you know…
And there's only one Frank Carter.

149
00:12:44,375 --> 00:12:48,750
Your case file mentioned an accomplice
to Carter who was never identified.

150
00:12:48,833 --> 00:12:51,333
I did. I did.
It was a theory, and it went cold.

151
00:12:51,416 --> 00:12:52,416
They often do.

152
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:02,875
Frank Carter still declines all interviews
via his lawyers.

153
00:13:02,958 --> 00:13:05,416
You remain the only one
he's ever agreed to speak with

154
00:13:05,500 --> 00:13:08,458
since his, uh, incarceration.

155
00:13:09,583 --> 00:13:11,375
Got any advice interviewing him?

156
00:13:11,458 --> 00:13:13,250
Yeah, I'd say don't.

157
00:13:16,041 --> 00:13:18,000
I… I hope you find your kid.

158
00:13:18,500 --> 00:13:21,375
With all due respect, sir,
hope does nothing for me.

159
00:13:27,875 --> 00:13:29,875
[unsettling music playing]

160
00:13:57,666 --> 00:14:00,625
Can I put this
in my Packet of Special Things?

161
00:14:00,708 --> 00:14:02,125
Let me see.

162
00:14:07,625 --> 00:14:08,458
Sure.

163
00:14:15,333 --> 00:14:16,541
What's that?

164
00:14:17,208 --> 00:14:19,791
We made our hands be in paint
on the wall at school.

165
00:14:19,875 --> 00:14:21,583
Oh, yeah? Handprints, huh?

166
00:14:21,666 --> 00:14:23,041
-[Jake] Mm-hmm.
-Cool.

167
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:24,500
My friend helped me.

168
00:14:26,291 --> 00:14:28,333
Oh, yeah? You make a friend?

169
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:31,041
The girl in the blue sweater.

170
00:14:33,250 --> 00:14:35,958
Well, do you remember
we talked about that?

171
00:14:36,041 --> 00:14:38,416
How some friends are pretend and…

172
00:14:42,458 --> 00:14:43,625
What's up, bud?

173
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,958
Are you sure she won't wake up?

174
00:14:48,041 --> 00:14:49,000
[Tom] Mommy?

175
00:14:50,416 --> 00:14:51,541
I am.

176
00:14:53,958 --> 00:14:56,291
You know, Mommy loved you

177
00:14:57,458 --> 00:15:01,625
more than anything, you know,
and that's… that's never gonna change.

178
00:15:02,166 --> 00:15:06,250
But it doesn't mean
that you can't make room for new people,

179
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:08,625
you know, new… new friends.

180
00:15:09,291 --> 00:15:11,833
I don't like the boys at school.

181
00:15:15,083 --> 00:15:16,000
You know,

182
00:15:16,916 --> 00:15:18,375
I never told you this,

183
00:15:18,458 --> 00:15:23,416
but when I was your age,
I had a friend, just like you have.

184
00:15:23,500 --> 00:15:24,416
I did.

185
00:15:24,500 --> 00:15:27,666
He'd visit me when I was going to sleep,
and we'd go on adventures.

186
00:15:28,333 --> 00:15:29,875
At the end, every time,

187
00:15:29,958 --> 00:15:32,375
he would kiss me on the forehead,
right here.

188
00:15:32,458 --> 00:15:33,541
And then

189
00:15:34,416 --> 00:15:38,375
I'd wake up the next morning
back in bed like magic.

190
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:41,375
I called him Mr. Night. [chuckles]

191
00:15:42,166 --> 00:15:43,250
[chuckles]

192
00:15:43,333 --> 00:15:46,208
It's okay to imagine things, Jake.

193
00:15:46,291 --> 00:15:48,041
You just… You gotta

194
00:15:48,958 --> 00:15:51,583
give real people a chance, too, okay?

195
00:16:04,958 --> 00:16:07,333
[high-pitched eerie music playing]

196
00:16:17,958 --> 00:16:19,541
[softly] What is your name?

197
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:27,083
[man whispers] It's okay.

198
00:16:28,208 --> 00:16:29,916
They need to hear this.

199
00:16:32,125 --> 00:16:34,958
[low thrumming]

200
00:16:37,666 --> 00:16:39,666
[eerie music building]

201
00:16:48,291 --> 00:16:50,500
[tense music playing]

202
00:17:01,416 --> 00:17:03,416
[indistinct background chatter]

203
00:17:22,250 --> 00:17:24,250
[music fades]

204
00:17:24,333 --> 00:17:26,625
[excited background chatter]

205
00:17:26,708 --> 00:17:29,291
[Tom] Hey! Sorry! Sorry, I'm late.

206
00:17:29,375 --> 00:17:32,333
-You're Jake's father?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. Hi. How you doing?

207
00:17:33,125 --> 00:17:34,500
Buddy, what's wrong?

208
00:17:34,583 --> 00:17:36,750
[woman] You wanna tell your dad
what happened?

209
00:17:37,541 --> 00:17:39,250
I got put on yellow.

210
00:17:39,333 --> 00:17:40,625
You… On what?

211
00:17:40,708 --> 00:17:43,208
We have a traffic light system
for bad behavior.

212
00:17:43,791 --> 00:17:45,916
What'd he do? Uh, what'd you do?

213
00:17:46,500 --> 00:17:49,125
Owen tried to take
my Packet of Special Things.

214
00:17:49,208 --> 00:17:51,583
He scratched a boy. Badly.

215
00:17:51,666 --> 00:17:54,875
Okay, well, that's…
You can't do that, Jake.

216
00:17:54,958 --> 00:17:57,416
Um, sorry. It's this packet.

217
00:17:57,500 --> 00:18:01,125
Um, it's full of stuff that,
like, belonged to his mom.

218
00:18:01,208 --> 00:18:02,666
That's no excuse.

219
00:18:03,500 --> 00:18:06,500
We'd like him to write a note apologizing.

220
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,666
Uh, isn't that excessive?

221
00:18:09,750 --> 00:18:12,250
We have zero tolerance
for kids hurting kids.

222
00:18:12,333 --> 00:18:13,875
What's your tolerance for bullies?

223
00:18:13,958 --> 00:18:16,416
'Cause that other kid
sounds like kind of a dick.

224
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:19,416
-[woman] Excuse me?
-You know what? We'll pass on that note.

225
00:18:19,500 --> 00:18:20,416
Come on, buddy.

226
00:18:21,583 --> 00:18:23,166
You can put me on yellow.

227
00:18:29,708 --> 00:18:30,666
[Beck] Where is it?

228
00:18:35,666 --> 00:18:38,750
[Neil] <i>I didn't like being there,</i>

229
00:18:38,833 --> 00:18:40,458
<i>that house.</i>

230
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:42,708
[man whispering] <i>Your grandmother's.</i>

231
00:18:43,583 --> 00:18:45,708
<i>Was she mean to you</i>?

232
00:18:46,750 --> 00:18:49,208
[Neil] <i>No. Sometimes</i>

233
00:18:49,833 --> 00:18:51,458
<i>she was sick.</i>

234
00:18:52,875 --> 00:18:54,375
<i>I was afraid.</i>

235
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,416
[man] <i>It's okay.</i>

236
00:18:57,208 --> 00:18:59,041
<i>They need to hear it.</i>

237
00:19:00,750 --> 00:19:03,083
[Neil] <i>I was afraid she'd die.</i>

238
00:19:03,166 --> 00:19:06,958
<i>She'd be dead in the house with me</i>
<i>while I slept.</i>

239
00:19:08,208 --> 00:19:11,333
[man] <i>If you could talk to your mommy</i>
<i>right now,</i>

240
00:19:12,250 --> 00:19:13,666
<i>what would you say?</i>

241
00:19:15,958 --> 00:19:18,083
[Neil] <i>Why did you leave me there?</i>

242
00:19:18,791 --> 00:19:20,583
<i>Why don't you love me?</i>

243
00:19:22,208 --> 00:19:23,625
[man] <i>I love you.</i>

244
00:19:26,250 --> 00:19:30,250
[on tape] <i>♪ Free your mind</i>
<i>And the rest will follow </i>♪

245
00:19:30,791 --> 00:19:33,166
♪ <i>Be color blind </i>♪

246
00:19:33,250 --> 00:19:34,916
<i>♪ Don't be so shallow ♪</i>

247
00:19:35,875 --> 00:19:39,916
<i>♪ Free your mind</i>
<i>And the rest will follow </i>♪

248
00:19:40,416 --> 00:19:41,416
[song ends]

249
00:19:50,583 --> 00:19:53,583
[wind howling]

250
00:19:56,125 --> 00:19:57,125
[soft thud]

251
00:19:58,000 --> 00:20:00,083
[tapping]

252
00:20:06,708 --> 00:20:09,708
[tapping]

253
00:20:09,791 --> 00:20:11,791
[wind continues howling]

254
00:20:15,583 --> 00:20:16,583
[soft thud]

255
00:20:22,416 --> 00:20:23,416
[thud]

256
00:20:41,333 --> 00:20:42,958
[ominous music]

257
00:20:51,166 --> 00:20:54,041
[Jake quietly]
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

258
00:20:54,125 --> 00:20:56,750
<i>Soon you'll hear the whispers spoken</i>

259
00:20:57,458 --> 00:20:59,625
<i>If your window is left unlatched</i>

260
00:20:59,708 --> 00:21:02,166
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

261
00:21:03,208 --> 00:21:04,250
Jake?

262
00:21:05,625 --> 00:21:06,833
What are you doing?

263
00:21:08,083 --> 00:21:10,083
[sinister music]

264
00:21:11,583 --> 00:21:12,500
Jake!

265
00:21:13,500 --> 00:21:14,625
No!

266
00:21:18,208 --> 00:21:20,208
[dramatic music playing]

267
00:21:27,625 --> 00:21:28,916
Who were you talking to?

268
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,333
Nobody.

269
00:21:34,041 --> 00:21:36,125
[wind howling]

270
00:21:36,208 --> 00:21:40,458
[slow tapping]

271
00:21:40,541 --> 00:21:42,291
[rattling]

272
00:21:45,291 --> 00:21:46,208
Back to bed.

273
00:21:47,708 --> 00:21:49,708
[tapping and creaking]

274
00:21:57,791 --> 00:22:01,625
[wind continues howling]

275
00:22:04,458 --> 00:22:07,458
[soft mysterious piano music playing]

276
00:22:20,750 --> 00:22:21,791
[thud]

277
00:22:25,500 --> 00:22:26,625
[sighs]

278
00:22:46,708 --> 00:22:47,750
[Tom] Hey!

279
00:22:50,791 --> 00:22:53,083
Hey! What are you doing?

280
00:22:53,166 --> 00:22:55,500
Hey! Hey! Hey!

281
00:22:55,583 --> 00:22:56,708
[grunts]

282
00:22:57,541 --> 00:22:59,541
[groans]

283
00:23:01,958 --> 00:23:05,791
[man] We've had reports of a squatter
since the place went vacant.

284
00:23:05,875 --> 00:23:09,958
Kids sneaking in to drink
and do other things.

285
00:23:10,041 --> 00:23:11,625
This wasn't a kid.

286
00:23:14,125 --> 00:23:15,000
What's back here?

287
00:23:16,583 --> 00:23:17,708
I don't know.

288
00:23:24,125 --> 00:23:26,041
-Holy shit.
-[officer] Ooh.

289
00:23:30,750 --> 00:23:32,083
-Whoa.
-Previous owner?

290
00:23:32,583 --> 00:23:33,541
Um…

291
00:23:35,166 --> 00:23:36,333
[Tom] So now what?

292
00:23:37,583 --> 00:23:39,208
Well, he didn't attack you.

293
00:23:39,291 --> 00:23:42,291
He just bolted for the door
unless there's something else.

294
00:23:42,375 --> 00:23:44,750
He's most likely just a squatter.

295
00:23:45,375 --> 00:23:46,833
Left something here.

296
00:23:46,916 --> 00:23:49,125
Didn't realize the place was rented.

297
00:23:49,208 --> 00:23:51,166
Change the locks,
set up a security system,

298
00:23:51,250 --> 00:23:53,333
and donate this stuff to the Goodwill.

299
00:23:53,833 --> 00:23:55,875
And don't forget to bolt your back door.

300
00:23:58,208 --> 00:23:59,291
So that's it?

301
00:23:59,791 --> 00:24:02,666
[officer] Fresh coat of paint
on the outside might help ward people off.

302
00:24:13,750 --> 00:24:15,750
[wind howling]

303
00:24:53,583 --> 00:24:56,250
[Jake] <i>If you're lonely, sad, and blue</i>

304
00:24:56,333 --> 00:24:58,666
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

305
00:24:58,750 --> 00:25:00,666
[soft pulsing music playing]

306
00:25:02,250 --> 00:25:04,875
[Jake talking softly on video]

307
00:25:04,958 --> 00:25:07,000
[Jake quietly] <i>If your window's</i>
<i>left unlatched</i>

308
00:25:07,083 --> 00:25:08,916
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the…</i>

309
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,583
Jake, what are you doing?

310
00:25:10,666 --> 00:25:11,875
Nothing.

311
00:25:12,458 --> 00:25:13,500
[Tom sighs]

312
00:25:13,583 --> 00:25:16,708
[wind howling]

313
00:25:17,458 --> 00:25:18,416
[Tom] Okay.

314
00:25:19,125 --> 00:25:20,500
Who are you talking to?

315
00:25:22,750 --> 00:25:24,333
Is it the girl in the blue sweater?

316
00:25:27,791 --> 00:25:30,708
She's scared of it here.

317
00:25:30,791 --> 00:25:33,208
She's scared of it here?
She's scared of this house? Why?

318
00:25:34,208 --> 00:25:36,250
She's scared of the boy who lives here.

319
00:25:37,416 --> 00:25:38,333
You?

320
00:25:40,125 --> 00:25:41,000
Who?

321
00:25:41,083 --> 00:25:42,458
The boy in the floor.

322
00:25:42,541 --> 00:25:44,958
The boy in the floor. Good God.

323
00:25:45,041 --> 00:25:47,333
Jake, you have to stop this.

324
00:25:47,416 --> 00:25:48,500
Stop what?

325
00:25:48,583 --> 00:25:51,000
Well… Ow! Goddammit!

326
00:25:52,541 --> 00:25:55,375
Pretending. I need you to grow up.

327
00:25:55,458 --> 00:25:57,041
You never believe me.

328
00:25:57,125 --> 00:25:58,250
[Tom] I can see you.

329
00:25:58,333 --> 00:25:59,833
I can see everything,

330
00:25:59,916 --> 00:26:03,041
and I know there is no one in here, Jake.

331
00:26:03,125 --> 00:26:05,750
You are just talking to yourself.

332
00:26:09,500 --> 00:26:10,375
[sighs]

333
00:26:22,750 --> 00:26:25,750
[high-pitched eerie music playing]

334
00:26:27,125 --> 00:26:28,125
[silence]

335
00:26:46,541 --> 00:26:48,541
[soft pulsing music playing]

336
00:26:51,208 --> 00:26:52,166
[Tom] Jake?

337
00:26:56,875 --> 00:26:57,791
Wha…

338
00:27:00,250 --> 00:27:02,250
[tense music playing]

339
00:27:05,875 --> 00:27:06,958
Jake?

340
00:27:09,875 --> 00:27:11,083
[yelling] Jake!

341
00:27:11,166 --> 00:27:12,041
Jake!

342
00:27:13,208 --> 00:27:14,166
Jake!

343
00:27:15,208 --> 00:27:16,166
Jake!

344
00:27:20,500 --> 00:27:21,916
Jake!

345
00:27:25,375 --> 00:27:26,291
Jake!

346
00:27:27,875 --> 00:27:29,958
Jake!

347
00:27:31,041 --> 00:27:32,208
Jake!

348
00:27:33,375 --> 00:27:34,416
Jake!

349
00:27:38,083 --> 00:27:40,083
[sirens wailing]

350
00:27:59,333 --> 00:28:02,375
I'm Detective Beck.
Tell me a little bit about Jake.

351
00:28:04,458 --> 00:28:05,416
Okay.

352
00:28:07,500 --> 00:28:08,416
[Beck] I know.

353
00:28:09,625 --> 00:28:11,375
-It's terrifying.
-[Tom moans softly]

354
00:28:11,458 --> 00:28:13,583
[breathes unsteadily]

355
00:28:13,666 --> 00:28:14,750
He's quiet.

356
00:28:15,250 --> 00:28:16,250
[Beck] It's hard.

357
00:28:17,375 --> 00:28:20,708
But we don't know which detail
is gonna help us find him.

358
00:28:24,166 --> 00:28:25,125
Okay.

359
00:28:28,541 --> 00:28:29,666
He, uh…

360
00:28:30,458 --> 00:28:33,125
He's a collector, you know, of…

361
00:28:34,791 --> 00:28:38,000
just, like, scraps of… of odds and ends.

362
00:28:38,083 --> 00:28:39,416
You know, like, um,

363
00:28:40,625 --> 00:28:44,875
ticket stubs and… and… and ribbon
and rocks even.

364
00:28:44,958 --> 00:28:47,250
It… it all has meaning to him.

365
00:28:47,333 --> 00:28:49,666
-That's nice.
-Yeah, he's a nice kid.

366
00:28:50,250 --> 00:28:51,333
What about his friends?

367
00:28:52,625 --> 00:28:53,541
[over radio] <i>Stand by.</i>

368
00:28:53,625 --> 00:28:57,875
We just moved, and, uh, you know,
school is just getting started, so…

369
00:28:58,541 --> 00:28:59,500
From where?

370
00:29:00,916 --> 00:29:04,125
-The Shore. Uh, Manasquan.
-[Beck] Hmm.

371
00:29:04,625 --> 00:29:06,500
Jake's mom grew up here, so…

372
00:29:06,583 --> 00:29:08,625
She's… gone.

373
00:29:09,583 --> 00:29:11,500
She was sick.

374
00:29:11,583 --> 00:29:13,583
[indistinct chatter over radio]

375
00:29:14,708 --> 00:29:16,666
Any other family nearby?

376
00:29:18,750 --> 00:29:19,791
My father.

377
00:29:19,875 --> 00:29:22,083
He's, uh… somewhere.

378
00:29:22,166 --> 00:29:23,916
I don't know. He's never met Jake.

379
00:29:25,750 --> 00:29:27,083
What's his name?

380
00:29:28,375 --> 00:29:31,291
Peter Willis. He was a cop.

381
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,041
And have you called him? Your father?

382
00:29:40,041 --> 00:29:41,000
No.

383
00:29:43,250 --> 00:29:45,000
We looked at the nanny cam,

384
00:29:46,166 --> 00:29:50,000
and he left on his own.
There was no one else.

385
00:29:50,541 --> 00:29:52,250
[Tom breathes shakily]

386
00:29:52,333 --> 00:29:54,333
[unsettling music playing]

387
00:29:57,250 --> 00:29:58,291
Detective.

388
00:30:03,500 --> 00:30:04,416
What the fuck?

389
00:30:05,666 --> 00:30:06,583
Jesus.

390
00:30:07,083 --> 00:30:09,083
[unsettling music building]

391
00:30:19,166 --> 00:30:21,291
[indistinct chatter over radio]

392
00:30:28,458 --> 00:30:29,458
[sniffs]

393
00:30:42,291 --> 00:30:44,833
[unsettling music continues]

394
00:30:54,375 --> 00:30:56,791
[phone ringing]

395
00:31:04,958 --> 00:31:05,958
[music fades]

396
00:31:06,041 --> 00:31:06,958
Hello?

397
00:31:07,916 --> 00:31:08,875
[Tom] <i>Dad?</i>

398
00:31:11,625 --> 00:31:13,375
[door opens, bell jingles]

399
00:31:40,041 --> 00:31:43,125
[footsteps approaching]

400
00:31:45,875 --> 00:31:47,000
[server] What can I get you?

401
00:31:47,916 --> 00:31:49,916
Uh, I'll just have a coffee, yeah.

402
00:31:50,541 --> 00:31:52,000
You want coffee?

403
00:31:53,125 --> 00:31:54,708
-[server] Two coffees?
-[Pete] Yeah.

404
00:32:04,791 --> 00:32:06,083
How you holding up?

405
00:32:11,375 --> 00:32:14,333
I just need to know
they're doing everything they can. Okay?

406
00:32:14,916 --> 00:32:16,458
I'm doing everything I can.

407
00:32:17,458 --> 00:32:18,333
Sure.

408
00:32:19,875 --> 00:32:21,875
At the department,
you still have friends there.

409
00:32:21,958 --> 00:32:23,500
I mean, you still have pull.

410
00:32:24,750 --> 00:32:27,958
I was young. I… I don't remember much.

411
00:32:28,708 --> 00:32:32,500
But I remember the Whisper Man,
and I remember you found him.

412
00:32:32,583 --> 00:32:34,000
I found him. I did do that.

413
00:32:34,083 --> 00:32:35,083
[server approaching]

414
00:32:35,166 --> 00:32:36,083
[Tom] So…

415
00:32:44,708 --> 00:32:45,791
He's a good kid, Jake.

416
00:32:45,875 --> 00:32:47,583
He's smart, and…

417
00:32:49,333 --> 00:32:50,875
They got any leads?

418
00:32:51,375 --> 00:32:53,541
Well, yeah, I mean,
if they'd fucking follow 'em.

419
00:32:53,625 --> 00:32:54,958
That's why I need you.

420
00:32:55,458 --> 00:32:57,916
Well, I'm sure they've got
a good detective working the case.

421
00:32:58,500 --> 00:33:00,541
No, <i>you </i>were a good detective.

422
00:33:00,625 --> 00:33:03,958
You're a shitty father,
but a good fucking detective.

423
00:33:04,041 --> 00:33:05,291
They will listen to you,

424
00:33:05,375 --> 00:33:07,916
and they will tell you things
they won't tell me.

425
00:33:08,000 --> 00:33:09,125
I, um…

426
00:33:09,208 --> 00:33:10,375
Well, uh…

427
00:33:12,916 --> 00:33:15,083
Listen, I… I…

428
00:33:16,458 --> 00:33:20,458
I wanted to reach out earlier,
especially after Rebecca had passed away--

429
00:33:20,541 --> 00:33:21,500
Don't.

430
00:33:23,250 --> 00:33:24,166
Don't do that.

431
00:33:28,250 --> 00:33:32,000
-Sorry it took this to get us together.
-We're not. This isn't us together.

432
00:33:32,083 --> 00:33:34,416
This is me asking you for help.
Do you understand that?

433
00:33:39,041 --> 00:33:40,458
Sure, I understand that.

434
00:33:43,291 --> 00:33:46,625
I don't know what I can do, Tom. I…

435
00:33:49,416 --> 00:33:52,291
I haven't carried a shield in forever.

436
00:33:52,875 --> 00:33:54,541
I'm sure they don't wanna hear from me.

437
00:33:55,541 --> 00:33:57,083
But I am here for you, whatever--

438
00:33:57,166 --> 00:34:00,708
Excuse me. I don't need
your emotional fucking support, okay?

439
00:34:00,791 --> 00:34:03,666
I need you to find my boy!

440
00:34:13,791 --> 00:34:14,625
No? Great.

441
00:34:19,791 --> 00:34:21,208
[door opens]

442
00:34:31,833 --> 00:34:32,833
[sighs]

443
00:34:40,208 --> 00:34:43,208
[indistinct chatter, phones ringing]

444
00:34:47,291 --> 00:34:51,208
[Beck] Why'd Carter do that?
The T-shirt. Cover their faces.

445
00:34:51,291 --> 00:34:54,750
[Pete] Didn't want them looking at him.
He didn't wanna look at them.

446
00:35:06,208 --> 00:35:09,041
There's, uh, not much new here.
This is all you have?

447
00:35:09,125 --> 00:35:10,416
We're still playing catch-up.

448
00:35:11,916 --> 00:35:13,625
And Tom said he gave you a lead?

449
00:35:13,708 --> 00:35:16,125
Yeah. We have a loose description
of a vagrant he saw

450
00:35:16,208 --> 00:35:18,916
rummaging around his basement.
Haven't found a match yet.

451
00:35:21,875 --> 00:35:24,000
Uh, you should listen to the Spencer tape.

452
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,541
[Pete] This is from the boy?
Blaming the parents.

453
00:35:27,625 --> 00:35:30,791
-Same as Frank Carter's Whisper Man.
-[Pete] Yeah, I've heard this.

454
00:35:30,875 --> 00:35:33,291
These kids aren't the only
intended victims.

455
00:35:33,375 --> 00:35:34,583
Forensics?

456
00:35:35,291 --> 00:35:38,541
The package was mishandled
at the TV station. It's tainted.

457
00:35:38,625 --> 00:35:41,916
Obviously, with the tape drop,
we know time is short.

458
00:35:44,875 --> 00:35:48,791
Tom said you never met him. Jake.

459
00:35:49,916 --> 00:35:50,875
May I ask why?

460
00:35:54,041 --> 00:35:58,208
Any connection between the two boys
other than they were found missing?

461
00:35:59,125 --> 00:36:00,833
Jake was new to town.

462
00:36:00,916 --> 00:36:03,291
Uh, different elementary
as the Spencer boy

463
00:36:03,375 --> 00:36:04,875
who went to Catholic school.

464
00:36:05,375 --> 00:36:07,958
Stevie Grant was in foster care.

465
00:36:09,250 --> 00:36:11,250
We're looking
at a few local sex offenders.

466
00:36:11,958 --> 00:36:15,333
You speculated in the Carter case
that the boys somehow

467
00:36:15,416 --> 00:36:17,291
walked out of their homes on their own.

468
00:36:17,375 --> 00:36:21,375
That Frank Carter… somehow summoned them.

469
00:36:22,375 --> 00:36:25,041
[Pete] Carter knew how to find
the ones who wanted to go.

470
00:36:25,125 --> 00:36:27,041
[unsettling music playing]

471
00:36:34,125 --> 00:36:35,291
[banging on door]

472
00:36:41,125 --> 00:36:42,083
From your house.

473
00:36:44,041 --> 00:36:46,541
What if my boy comes back home
and I'm not there?

474
00:36:47,041 --> 00:36:50,666
It's a crime scene.
Right now, this is best.

475
00:36:51,291 --> 00:36:53,208
Unless you have someone you can stay with.

476
00:37:13,708 --> 00:37:16,250
[tense music playing]

477
00:37:24,875 --> 00:37:26,208
[cell phone ringing]

478
00:37:26,875 --> 00:37:27,708
Beck here.

479
00:37:27,791 --> 00:37:31,666
The man who used to live in my house
did time at the East Jersey State Prison.

480
00:37:31,750 --> 00:37:32,583
[Beck] <i>Mr. Kennedy?</i>

481
00:37:33,208 --> 00:37:35,083
[Tom] <i>Yeah, I have his mail right here.</i>

482
00:37:35,166 --> 00:37:37,916
Dominic Barnett,
assaulting a police officer.

483
00:37:38,000 --> 00:37:40,750
-He got out fucking seven years ago.
-[Beck] <i>Slow down.</i>

484
00:37:40,833 --> 00:37:43,208
You're saying he lived at the house
that you're renting?

485
00:37:43,291 --> 00:37:45,250
It could be him.
Look, they were both at Rahway.

486
00:37:45,333 --> 00:37:47,333
And if he knew Carter
while they were inside--

487
00:37:47,416 --> 00:37:48,750
[Beck] <i>Uh, send me what you have,</i>

488
00:37:48,833 --> 00:37:51,291
okay, and I'll look into it.
Uh, Dominic Barnett, you say?

489
00:37:52,416 --> 00:37:54,541
This could be the guy.

490
00:37:54,625 --> 00:37:56,125
I said I'll look into it.

491
00:37:56,208 --> 00:37:57,541
<i>Okay? Thank you.</i>

492
00:37:57,625 --> 00:37:59,500
Are you… are you fucking kid…

493
00:38:00,583 --> 00:38:01,583
-[phone clatters]
-Fuck!

494
00:38:01,666 --> 00:38:03,083
Barnett, I know that name.

495
00:38:03,166 --> 00:38:07,125
He was a runner for the Brick Squad gang
back when I was on the job.

496
00:38:07,208 --> 00:38:09,833
[Beck] Yeah, they deal
out of the Wrigley Projects now.

497
00:38:09,916 --> 00:38:12,666
And how long between the time
when the kids were put to bed

498
00:38:12,750 --> 00:38:14,083
and when they disappeared?

499
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:17,125
For the Spencer boy, not long.
Ninety minutes.

500
00:38:17,208 --> 00:38:18,291
Jake?

501
00:38:18,791 --> 00:38:21,250
Six hours before Tom woke up.

502
00:38:22,166 --> 00:38:24,416
He was drinking, maybe drunk.

503
00:38:24,500 --> 00:38:26,166
I could smell the alcohol.

504
00:38:28,291 --> 00:38:29,833
[Pete] I never met her.

505
00:38:29,916 --> 00:38:33,708
She called once,
wanted to tell me that she was pregnant.

506
00:38:35,125 --> 00:38:36,375
We talked for a bit.

507
00:38:38,041 --> 00:38:39,208
He was in good hands.

508
00:38:47,500 --> 00:38:48,875
Drawing wars.

509
00:38:49,375 --> 00:38:50,833
Tom did these too.

510
00:38:52,625 --> 00:38:54,791
You never know what gets passed on.

511
00:38:56,458 --> 00:38:58,458
[wind chimes tinkling]

512
00:38:59,583 --> 00:39:02,333
[dog barking]

513
00:39:02,416 --> 00:39:03,416
[woman] Hey!

514
00:39:03,500 --> 00:39:06,541
Mrs. Shearing.
I'm the guy renting your house.

515
00:39:06,625 --> 00:39:08,000
Tom. Tom Kennedy.

516
00:39:08,083 --> 00:39:10,041
You said you'd clear that shit out!

517
00:39:10,125 --> 00:39:11,291
-I'm not doing it for you!
-No!

518
00:39:11,375 --> 00:39:14,250
-Mrs. Shearing, please! My son is missing!
-Fuck off, Randall.

519
00:39:14,333 --> 00:39:15,416
[Tom] Please!

520
00:39:16,083 --> 00:39:17,916
[Beck] We should still interview him.

521
00:39:18,416 --> 00:39:21,541
Carter. He won't see anyone
unless you're there.

522
00:39:21,625 --> 00:39:26,208
[Pete] Yeah, all that bastard will do is
make you nauseous and want to throw up.

523
00:39:26,291 --> 00:39:27,791
When we zeroed in on him,

524
00:39:27,875 --> 00:39:30,500
Carter had managed
a day and a half on the run.

525
00:39:30,583 --> 00:39:32,208
And when we finally did get him,

526
00:39:32,291 --> 00:39:35,583
there was evidence that the fifth boy
he took, Tony Smith, was still alive.

527
00:39:36,083 --> 00:39:38,125
I did everything I could to find him.
Everything.

528
00:39:38,208 --> 00:39:41,000
I interrogated Carter's wife
at least six hours.

529
00:39:41,083 --> 00:39:42,791
And then I went to see Carter himself

530
00:39:42,875 --> 00:39:45,750
to appeal to what little bit of humanity
might be left in him.

531
00:39:45,833 --> 00:39:47,000
There was nothing.

532
00:39:48,375 --> 00:39:49,291
Nothing.

533
00:39:50,208 --> 00:39:53,125
Dominic Barnett. You rented to him?

534
00:39:53,208 --> 00:39:56,791
That nephew of mine ain't worth fuck all.

535
00:39:56,875 --> 00:39:58,250
Wait, you're related?

536
00:39:58,333 --> 00:40:01,583
Little shit up and cleared out
without paying six months' rent.

537
00:40:01,666 --> 00:40:05,375
Okay, is there anything you can tell me
about where to find him now?

538
00:40:07,750 --> 00:40:12,208
He had a girlfriend
at the Wrigley Park Projects.

539
00:40:12,291 --> 00:40:15,166
Okay, do you know her name,
the girlfriend?

540
00:40:17,083 --> 00:40:19,041
Tina… Tiffany.

541
00:40:19,125 --> 00:40:22,000
I do remember she lived… [laughs]

542
00:40:22,750 --> 00:40:24,708
…in Building C.

543
00:40:24,791 --> 00:40:26,208
For "cunt."

544
00:40:26,958 --> 00:40:28,958
[siren wailing in background]

545
00:40:36,500 --> 00:40:39,666
-[music playing over speakers]
-[indistinct chatter]

546
00:40:57,916 --> 00:40:59,625
[man shouting] Hey, yo, my peeps!

547
00:41:00,625 --> 00:41:01,625
Everybody out here!

548
00:41:13,333 --> 00:41:15,166
[indistinct voices in background]

549
00:41:15,250 --> 00:41:16,583
[door slams]

550
00:41:16,666 --> 00:41:17,708
[dog barking]

551
00:41:17,791 --> 00:41:19,791
[indistinct shouting]

552
00:41:21,750 --> 00:41:24,625
[man] How the fuck you don't hear me
when I'm fucking talking to you?!

553
00:41:24,708 --> 00:41:26,333
Look at me when I'm talking to you!

554
00:41:26,416 --> 00:41:30,291
[man continues shouting]

555
00:41:32,875 --> 00:41:34,708
[tense music playing]

556
00:41:34,791 --> 00:41:37,333
-Help you?
-Uh, no. No, thanks.

557
00:41:37,416 --> 00:41:38,916
What are you looking for?

558
00:41:39,916 --> 00:41:41,208
Dominic Barnett.

559
00:41:41,291 --> 00:41:42,958
Don't know no Barnett.

560
00:41:43,041 --> 00:41:44,416
-[woman] Nah.
-Okay.

561
00:41:49,208 --> 00:41:50,708
Are you buying, motherfucker?

562
00:41:51,458 --> 00:41:52,958
Apache, Murder 8.

563
00:41:53,458 --> 00:41:55,250
Ten for one. Three for twenty.

564
00:41:55,333 --> 00:41:56,625
Fentanyl, bitch.

565
00:41:56,708 --> 00:41:58,916
Oh, uh, no. No, thanks.

566
00:42:00,875 --> 00:42:02,708
[both grunt]

567
00:42:02,791 --> 00:42:05,916
Beat your motherfucking ass.
The fuck you think you doing? Huh?

568
00:42:06,000 --> 00:42:07,250
[man grunts]

569
00:42:07,333 --> 00:42:11,083
Both of you, get the fuck out of here.
I'll blow your head off, motherfucker.

570
00:42:11,166 --> 00:42:12,375
All right. Get up.

571
00:42:14,875 --> 00:42:17,375
[tense music continues]

572
00:42:19,708 --> 00:42:21,416
-What about my car--
-Get in. Get in.

573
00:42:23,583 --> 00:42:25,375
[man 2] Yo, get the fuck outta here.

574
00:42:31,333 --> 00:42:34,333
Give me the keys. I'll get somebody
to pick up the car. Just give me the keys.

575
00:42:37,541 --> 00:42:39,875
[Tom] Jesus fucking Christ.

576
00:42:39,958 --> 00:42:41,708
What the fuck? How are you here?

577
00:42:41,791 --> 00:42:45,208
You were right to wanna look at Barnett,
but you gotta trust these detectives.

578
00:42:45,291 --> 00:42:46,500
Let 'em do their job.

579
00:42:46,583 --> 00:42:48,583
And that Detective Beck?
She's not gonna let this go.

580
00:42:48,666 --> 00:42:49,958
-You talked to her?
-[Pete] Yes--

581
00:42:50,041 --> 00:42:52,625
-You talked to her?
-I was with her when you called.

582
00:42:54,125 --> 00:42:55,291
-You were?
-[Pete] I was.

583
00:42:55,375 --> 00:42:56,583
[Tom] You were?

584
00:42:56,666 --> 00:42:58,750
No, somebody else was.
I was with her, yes.

585
00:43:00,833 --> 00:43:02,125
I'm on it.

586
00:43:02,708 --> 00:43:03,666
Okay.

587
00:43:07,083 --> 00:43:10,083
You know, when I heard you wrote novels,
I wasn't surprised

588
00:43:10,166 --> 00:43:11,625
'cause you were always creative.

589
00:43:11,708 --> 00:43:13,708
Can we not do this right now?

590
00:43:13,791 --> 00:43:15,291
What are you talking about?

591
00:43:15,375 --> 00:43:17,500
[Tom] Can we not talk about
my fucking novel?

592
00:43:17,583 --> 00:43:21,416
-What are you talking about?
-Jake is who I want you to focus on. Jake.

593
00:43:21,500 --> 00:43:23,750
Not us, not me. Jake.

594
00:43:23,833 --> 00:43:26,458
I checked on Barnett. Nowhere to be found.

595
00:43:26,541 --> 00:43:28,666
Not a word from him
in the last six months.

596
00:43:29,875 --> 00:43:31,875
Okay, so what? We're back to nothing?

597
00:43:31,958 --> 00:43:34,250
Just a tape, and then a body,
and then another tape?

598
00:43:34,333 --> 00:43:35,833
I remember how it went with Carter.

599
00:43:35,916 --> 00:43:38,833
He's irrelevant.
He's doing life in prison. Doesn't matter.

600
00:43:38,916 --> 00:43:40,250
Tell that to my boy.

601
00:43:42,458 --> 00:43:45,375
What if whoever took Jake
knows he's your grandson?

602
00:43:46,333 --> 00:43:49,333
A different last name.
There's no connection to the Spencer kid.

603
00:43:49,416 --> 00:43:51,916
Absolutely no connection whatsoever.

604
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:55,583
Yeah, but someone could find out.
I mean, Carter could be directing them.

605
00:43:56,625 --> 00:43:58,333
No, that's… that's going too far.

606
00:43:59,875 --> 00:44:01,875
Okay, but you're gonna go
talk to him, right?

607
00:44:01,958 --> 00:44:05,000
He'd just steer us in another direction,
in the wrong direction.

608
00:44:05,083 --> 00:44:07,333
So go, outsmart him.
You've done it once before.

609
00:44:07,416 --> 00:44:09,416
I didn't outsmart anything.
I just got lucky.

610
00:44:09,500 --> 00:44:12,125
So go get lucky again. What's the problem?

611
00:44:12,916 --> 00:44:16,125
-What, are you afraid of him?
-That man destroyed my life, my family.

612
00:44:16,208 --> 00:44:19,541
-You're damn right I'm afraid of him.
-No. You can't blame that on him.

613
00:44:19,625 --> 00:44:20,916
That was you.

614
00:44:25,125 --> 00:44:26,125
[door slams]

615
00:44:27,458 --> 00:44:28,916
[scribbling]

616
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:31,125
[lock clicks, door opens]

617
00:44:37,291 --> 00:44:38,291
[door closes]

618
00:44:38,375 --> 00:44:40,375
[foreboding music playing]

619
00:44:43,833 --> 00:44:47,250
[Pete on tape] <i>Your husband threatened you</i>
<i>when you started asking questions.</i>

620
00:44:49,416 --> 00:44:52,750
<i>Did he ever give off any hints</i>
<i>about what he was doing before that?</i>

621
00:44:56,625 --> 00:44:59,000
<i>Behaviors out of step with his routine?</i>

622
00:44:59,083 --> 00:45:01,833
<i>Places he'd go? Objects in the house?</i>

623
00:45:02,333 --> 00:45:04,625
<i>Even days he smelled different,</i>
<i>or his clothes were soiled</i>

624
00:45:04,708 --> 00:45:06,708
<i>in a way that couldn't be explained?</i>

625
00:45:08,041 --> 00:45:11,000
<i>I'm asking all this</i>
<i>because there's still another boy missing.</i>

626
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:14,208
<i>Tony Smith. He might still be alive.</i>

627
00:45:14,291 --> 00:45:15,416
[door opens]

628
00:45:15,500 --> 00:45:17,708
[Pete] <i>Frank put him somewhere,</i>
<i>and he's not talking.</i>

629
00:45:18,291 --> 00:45:20,000
<i>Maybe you can help us find him.</i>

630
00:45:21,208 --> 00:45:26,541
[cell phone buzzing]

631
00:45:27,041 --> 00:45:29,000
<i>-I've told you everything I know.</i>
-Yeah.

632
00:45:29,083 --> 00:45:31,083
[tense music playing]

633
00:46:17,083 --> 00:46:19,166
-[Pete] I'm here to see Beck.
-[man] Need some ID.

634
00:46:19,250 --> 00:46:20,375
[Beck] Let him through!

635
00:46:24,125 --> 00:46:25,291
Neil Spencer.

636
00:46:29,041 --> 00:46:30,041
No cameras?

637
00:46:31,041 --> 00:46:32,833
No. Not in the park.

638
00:46:36,375 --> 00:46:39,583
Could you check his nails, please?
His fingernails.

639
00:46:40,583 --> 00:46:41,583
Thank you.

640
00:46:43,208 --> 00:46:44,500
Carter would…

641
00:46:44,583 --> 00:46:47,541
He'd always cut their fingernails
before he strangled them.

642
00:46:48,083 --> 00:46:50,125
He didn't want them scratching his face.

643
00:46:50,208 --> 00:46:51,500
[Beck] Jesus.

644
00:46:53,833 --> 00:46:55,750
[camera shutter clicking]

645
00:46:55,833 --> 00:46:57,833
[indistinct chatter over radio]

646
00:46:58,458 --> 00:46:59,750
[over radio] <i>Copy that. Stand by.</i>

647
00:47:00,291 --> 00:47:01,250
What?

648
00:47:02,750 --> 00:47:03,875
Um…

649
00:47:05,541 --> 00:47:08,416
The shirt, the tapes.
That was all pretty much out there.

650
00:47:08,500 --> 00:47:09,833
It was all public.

651
00:47:10,916 --> 00:47:13,333
But not the cutting of the fingernails.
That wasn't public.

652
00:47:13,416 --> 00:47:16,875
Your accomplice theory, then.
Somebody who helped him back in the day.

653
00:47:18,000 --> 00:47:21,208
Well, why wait all these years
to get back to work?

654
00:47:27,916 --> 00:47:29,208
[sobbing]

655
00:47:34,375 --> 00:47:36,375
[stirring music playing]

656
00:47:49,041 --> 00:47:51,041
[music building]

657
00:48:07,541 --> 00:48:09,500
[stirring music continues]

658
00:48:40,250 --> 00:48:41,875
[door buzzes]

659
00:49:08,666 --> 00:49:10,083
[music fades]

660
00:49:10,166 --> 00:49:12,541
[Carter] You're a good man, Henry. Thanks.

661
00:49:19,875 --> 00:49:20,916
[door clangs]

662
00:49:21,000 --> 00:49:22,875
-Frank.
-Hi, Pete.

663
00:49:25,583 --> 00:49:26,875
Looking good.

664
00:49:26,958 --> 00:49:29,166
Thank you, Pete. Thank you.

665
00:49:29,250 --> 00:49:32,041
You know, 20, 30 years in the cage.

666
00:49:32,125 --> 00:49:34,333
Well, that'll keep you lean.

667
00:49:35,041 --> 00:49:35,958
Yeah.

668
00:49:37,958 --> 00:49:39,166
You still on the wagon?

669
00:49:41,041 --> 00:49:42,125
Good.

670
00:49:43,166 --> 00:49:44,916
That's very good. Really.

671
00:49:46,666 --> 00:49:49,916
I'm proud of you. If that means anything.

672
00:49:50,833 --> 00:49:52,500
'Cause, you know, whatever it is…

673
00:49:52,583 --> 00:49:54,333
[inhales, exhales sharply]

674
00:49:54,833 --> 00:49:57,375
…you know, your vice,

675
00:49:58,625 --> 00:50:00,916
you can try to lock it away,

676
00:50:01,000 --> 00:50:03,125
you can try to burn it
to the fucking ground,

677
00:50:03,208 --> 00:50:05,000
but it can't be killed.

678
00:50:05,083 --> 00:50:07,583
I mean, you can't kill it. You can't.

679
00:50:07,666 --> 00:50:10,458
Because it's like this guide or something.

680
00:50:10,541 --> 00:50:11,458
Right?

681
00:50:11,958 --> 00:50:16,166
I mean, it kind of takes hold of you
and controls you,

682
00:50:16,250 --> 00:50:18,125
and it becomes really

683
00:50:19,250 --> 00:50:23,333
the only thing in the world that exists.

684
00:50:23,875 --> 00:50:25,291
Everything else is just…

685
00:50:28,166 --> 00:50:29,125
window dressing.

686
00:50:29,208 --> 00:50:30,791
Kind of sad, really.

687
00:50:31,291 --> 00:50:32,750
How's that, Frank?

688
00:50:32,833 --> 00:50:34,375
Well, it's sad for you, isn't it?

689
00:50:34,458 --> 00:50:39,333
When you can't do the very thing

690
00:50:39,416 --> 00:50:41,666
that you were meant to do.

691
00:50:43,583 --> 00:50:44,500
I don't know.

692
00:50:46,208 --> 00:50:48,000
Might be better to just end it all.

693
00:50:50,291 --> 00:50:52,708
You could try that. Nobody'd miss you.

694
00:50:53,791 --> 00:50:55,875
A fair point. That's a fair point.

695
00:50:55,958 --> 00:50:57,000
I mean, yeah.

696
00:50:57,083 --> 00:51:00,083
But… but, I mean, for you, really, I mean…

697
00:51:03,708 --> 00:51:05,916
mostly it was endings, really.

698
00:51:06,500 --> 00:51:07,458
You know?

699
00:51:08,125 --> 00:51:11,166
Right? I mean, marriage, career,

700
00:51:12,208 --> 00:51:13,750
fatherhood. That didn't…

701
00:51:14,916 --> 00:51:17,625
Yeah, it's kind of like one long

702
00:51:18,500 --> 00:51:22,000
dirge on the road to your grave, right?

703
00:51:24,458 --> 00:51:26,666
Well, I'm hoping for a resurrection.

704
00:51:27,791 --> 00:51:29,250
Yours is unexpected.

705
00:51:29,916 --> 00:51:31,875
-[Carter chuckles]
-[Pete] Friend of yours?

706
00:51:32,458 --> 00:51:33,666
Friends? No.

707
00:51:36,666 --> 00:51:38,875
Men like you and I
don't have friends, Pete.

708
00:51:40,250 --> 00:51:41,583
We're meant to be alone.

709
00:51:41,666 --> 00:51:42,833
What else is there?

710
00:51:45,291 --> 00:51:47,333
-It speaks.
-[Beck] The work.

711
00:51:48,083 --> 00:51:49,791
It's all that's left, what you've done.

712
00:51:50,708 --> 00:51:53,625
This copycat, whoever he is,
he's showing you up.

713
00:51:54,375 --> 00:51:57,416
And if he keeps getting lucky, killing,

714
00:51:58,083 --> 00:51:59,708
what happens to your myth?

715
00:51:59,791 --> 00:52:01,458
You'll be replaced.

716
00:52:04,916 --> 00:52:06,166
She's pretty eager.

717
00:52:07,375 --> 00:52:09,791
What do you think, Pete?
How do you think she'll fare?

718
00:52:09,875 --> 00:52:11,291
As well as you?

719
00:52:12,250 --> 00:52:14,458
You should have seen him. Oh boy.

720
00:52:16,125 --> 00:52:17,250
Back then,

721
00:52:18,583 --> 00:52:21,416
so vital, so much life to live.

722
00:52:21,500 --> 00:52:23,666
He… Now, you know…

723
00:52:25,666 --> 00:52:26,625
you're all alone,

724
00:52:26,708 --> 00:52:29,500
cooking up your little dinners
in the dark.

725
00:52:29,583 --> 00:52:30,958
You know? I don't know.

726
00:52:33,041 --> 00:52:34,125
What do you think?

727
00:52:35,583 --> 00:52:37,458
Did it all turn out the way you'd hoped?

728
00:52:38,416 --> 00:52:39,333
You're here.

729
00:52:39,916 --> 00:52:40,833
Yeah.

730
00:52:42,833 --> 00:52:44,416
You gonna take credit for that?

731
00:52:44,500 --> 00:52:46,541
-Yes, I am. And comfort.
-[Carter] Okay.

732
00:52:46,625 --> 00:52:47,666
Okay.

733
00:52:48,833 --> 00:52:50,166
The killing stopped.

734
00:52:50,833 --> 00:52:52,708
The killing has stopped. [chuckles]

735
00:52:55,375 --> 00:52:56,875
But they haven't, have they?

736
00:52:56,958 --> 00:52:59,333
You know who's doing this, don't you?

737
00:53:02,250 --> 00:53:05,166
I'll tell you what.
You bring me my family, I might remember.

738
00:53:05,250 --> 00:53:06,333
Your family?

739
00:53:06,416 --> 00:53:07,541
My family. Tell her.

740
00:53:08,333 --> 00:53:09,500
Go ahead. Tell her, Pete.

741
00:53:09,583 --> 00:53:12,291
Tell her about my fucking family,

742
00:53:12,375 --> 00:53:13,916
how they sold me out.

743
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:15,833
[breathes heavily]

744
00:53:15,916 --> 00:53:16,916
I'll tell you what.

745
00:53:17,541 --> 00:53:20,041
Why don't you bring me my wife

746
00:53:20,750 --> 00:53:21,833
and my son?

747
00:53:23,333 --> 00:53:25,166
Just bring them to me for…

748
00:53:27,833 --> 00:53:30,041
five minutes.
Just leave me alone with them.

749
00:53:30,750 --> 00:53:33,291
Go ahead. Five minutes.
I'll tell you everything you wanna know.

750
00:53:33,375 --> 00:53:36,833
I'll whisper it
right in your really cute little ear.

751
00:53:37,833 --> 00:53:39,833
Five minutes alone. Me and them.

752
00:53:41,458 --> 00:53:44,083
Hmm, don't worry about clean-up.
Clean-up's easy.

753
00:53:45,500 --> 00:53:47,083
Just hose down the room.

754
00:53:47,166 --> 00:53:48,416
[Pete] Okay, we're done.

755
00:53:49,958 --> 00:53:52,166
[Carter] You don't wanna hear about
the sixth victim?

756
00:53:52,666 --> 00:53:53,666
-Come on!
-Tony Smith?

757
00:53:53,750 --> 00:53:56,625
Tony Smith was five.
Come on, keep up. Tell her.

758
00:53:56,708 --> 00:53:58,708
You know, this guy's
still out there chasing him.

759
00:53:58,791 --> 00:54:01,166
He's on the ball.
He's out there chasing him still.

760
00:54:01,250 --> 00:54:03,416
I'm not playing your games this time.

761
00:54:03,500 --> 00:54:05,458
Yeah, well, your son is.
Boy, he is all in.

762
00:54:05,541 --> 00:54:07,375
How about those books of his, huh?

763
00:54:07,458 --> 00:54:11,041
The detective character.
Boy, he is trying to be you.

764
00:54:11,125 --> 00:54:14,625
Oh, he wants to be daddy.
But, you know, that's how it goes.

765
00:54:15,250 --> 00:54:17,916
'Cause when you're denied
your father's love,

766
00:54:19,291 --> 00:54:21,208
of course you mythologize him.

767
00:54:22,541 --> 00:54:25,250
She'll find out who we're talking about.

768
00:54:26,750 --> 00:54:28,333
Who you've become.

769
00:54:29,666 --> 00:54:31,250
[door buzzes]

770
00:54:31,333 --> 00:54:34,666
What did he mean back there?
His sixth victim?

771
00:54:40,666 --> 00:54:42,208
I asked you a question.

772
00:54:47,125 --> 00:54:51,708
First week Tony Smith was missing,
a thousand cops were searching for him.

773
00:54:52,750 --> 00:54:54,750
A month later, a hundred.

774
00:54:54,833 --> 00:54:57,250
A year after that, a dozen.

775
00:54:58,583 --> 00:55:01,125
Now there's only one.

776
00:55:02,458 --> 00:55:03,333
Me.

777
00:55:06,375 --> 00:55:08,208
[tape crackling]

778
00:55:08,291 --> 00:55:12,291
[whispering] Is there anything else
you want to say to your daddy?

779
00:55:23,291 --> 00:55:25,291
[foreboding music playing]

780
00:55:34,666 --> 00:55:37,000
[Jake] Why didn't you believe me?

781
00:55:39,083 --> 00:55:41,375
[man] Visitor rolls
for East Jersey State Prison.

782
00:55:41,458 --> 00:55:42,583
Checking for repeats.

783
00:55:42,666 --> 00:55:45,416
Cross-referencing criminal records,
connections to Carter.

784
00:55:45,500 --> 00:55:48,041
Good. I want every match released
in the last five years,

785
00:55:48,125 --> 00:55:50,916
and someone needs to reach out
to the FBI's field office in Phoenix.

786
00:55:51,000 --> 00:55:52,666
I'm sorry, what's in Phoenix?

787
00:55:52,750 --> 00:55:55,541
Carter's wife and kid are in
the witness protection program there.

788
00:55:55,625 --> 00:55:58,333
So if Carter is having someone else
do his killings for him,

789
00:55:58,416 --> 00:56:00,416
we need to let them know
as soon as possible.

790
00:56:15,416 --> 00:56:16,875
-You find something?
-[Pete] Maybe.

791
00:56:16,958 --> 00:56:19,750
Norman Collins visited Rahway last March,

792
00:56:19,833 --> 00:56:22,375
a few times last year.

793
00:56:28,916 --> 00:56:30,250
I think you should take him.

794
00:56:34,750 --> 00:56:39,458
Mr. Collins, Detective Amanda Beck.
Garretton PD. Can I come in?

795
00:56:39,541 --> 00:56:41,208
-Absolutely.
-[Beck] Okay.

796
00:56:43,333 --> 00:56:46,041
[lively operatic music playing
over stereo]

797
00:56:57,500 --> 00:57:00,291
[Beck] You recently went to see
an inmate at Rahway Prison.

798
00:57:00,375 --> 00:57:02,916
Victor Tyler, yes.

799
00:57:03,500 --> 00:57:04,791
May I ask why?

800
00:57:04,875 --> 00:57:07,666
[operatic music continues]

801
00:57:07,750 --> 00:57:09,208
He's a fascinating man.

802
00:57:10,291 --> 00:57:13,833
Life for kidnapping and murder.
You find that fascinating?

803
00:57:16,416 --> 00:57:20,166
This was worn by
a fairly notorious murderer in the 1960s.

804
00:57:20,666 --> 00:57:24,500
It cost me a small fortune,
but it's such a handsome piece.

805
00:57:25,291 --> 00:57:27,500
And the provenance is inviolable.

806
00:57:27,583 --> 00:57:30,375
[music continues playing over speakers]

807
00:57:32,458 --> 00:57:34,500
All completely above board.

808
00:57:39,208 --> 00:57:40,333
[music stops]

809
00:57:40,416 --> 00:57:42,833
I'm very well respected in my field.

810
00:57:43,958 --> 00:57:45,500
What field is that?

811
00:57:45,583 --> 00:57:47,875
I'm a collector, like you.

812
00:57:48,875 --> 00:57:52,375
You have your perps,
your cases, your obsessions.

813
00:57:52,458 --> 00:57:58,083
When ugly things happen to nice people,
you want to know why and where and who.

814
00:57:58,166 --> 00:58:03,958
For me, the interest is more
in the "how" and the "what."

815
00:58:04,791 --> 00:58:05,708
No, thanks.

816
00:58:06,791 --> 00:58:09,708
Come on. We're humoring each other.

817
00:58:16,583 --> 00:58:17,750
Can you feel that?

818
00:58:18,791 --> 00:58:19,708
What?

819
00:58:21,791 --> 00:58:23,375
What it must have been like

820
00:58:23,875 --> 00:58:27,791
stabbing your husband 46 times
in front of your best friends

821
00:58:27,875 --> 00:58:29,833
over a lost hand of bridge.

822
00:58:30,333 --> 00:58:31,166
[Beck scoffs]

823
00:58:32,125 --> 00:58:33,291
[screwdriver clatters]

824
00:58:34,291 --> 00:58:36,291
Where were you the night of April 10th?

825
00:58:38,875 --> 00:58:40,875
-Traveling.
-To?

826
00:58:40,958 --> 00:58:42,875
[Collins] Boston for an exhibition.

827
00:58:43,375 --> 00:58:45,583
[Beck] Do you have anything
to substantiate that?

828
00:58:53,875 --> 00:58:57,041
I didn't have anything to do with
those children being taken, Detective,

829
00:58:57,125 --> 00:58:58,708
if that's what you're here about.

830
00:59:14,125 --> 00:59:15,958
Well, well, well.

831
00:59:16,791 --> 00:59:18,416
What the fuck you want?

832
00:59:18,500 --> 00:59:22,166
Mr. Tyler, a man named Norman Collins
visited you about six months ago,

833
00:59:22,250 --> 00:59:23,625
twice in one week.

834
00:59:23,708 --> 00:59:25,958
I got no say who comes to see me.

835
00:59:28,208 --> 00:59:29,458
Obviously.

836
00:59:31,625 --> 00:59:34,791
You raped
and you murdered a 12-year-old girl.

837
00:59:34,875 --> 00:59:36,125
[Tyler] Hmm.

838
00:59:36,208 --> 00:59:39,125
I think you got a pretty good situation
here for doing something like that.

839
00:59:39,208 --> 00:59:40,541
Yeah.

840
00:59:40,625 --> 00:59:42,416
It's my winning personality.

841
00:59:42,500 --> 00:59:46,416
Did you ever pass anything
between Norman Collins and Frank Carter?

842
00:59:47,500 --> 00:59:48,833
Who's Frank Carter?

843
00:59:50,750 --> 00:59:53,000
[laughing]

844
00:59:56,250 --> 00:59:58,000
Maybe this will jog your memory.

845
01:00:00,291 --> 01:00:01,125
Hmm.

846
01:00:05,916 --> 01:00:06,833
Hmm?

847
01:00:06,916 --> 01:00:10,750
Why don't you two little piggies
take your bullshit deal

848
01:00:10,833 --> 01:00:13,375
and cry wee-wee-wee-wee all the way home?

849
01:00:13,458 --> 01:00:15,041
It's not a deal.

850
01:00:15,125 --> 01:00:17,750
It's an interstate
prisoner transfer order.

851
01:00:18,541 --> 01:00:22,208
[Pete] I don't know what life's gonna
be like for you in Lewisburg, Mr. Tyler,

852
01:00:22,291 --> 01:00:26,208
but I don't think it's gonna be very good
for a child rapist.

853
01:00:26,291 --> 01:00:29,000
But you're gonna need someone
like Frank Carter to protect you.

854
01:00:29,500 --> 01:00:31,541
Otherwise,
you're gonna have a big problem.

855
01:00:31,625 --> 01:00:33,291
[Beck] You feel like talking now?

856
01:00:35,083 --> 01:00:37,708
[cell phone buzzing]

857
01:00:38,291 --> 01:00:39,458
Dyson, talk to me.

858
01:00:39,541 --> 01:00:40,583
[Dyson] Another package.

859
01:00:40,666 --> 01:00:43,375
The address was recognized
before it was pulled from a box.

860
01:00:43,458 --> 01:00:45,000
I don't want anybody knowing about this.

861
01:00:46,250 --> 01:00:47,250
Already on it.

862
01:00:47,333 --> 01:00:49,333
Jake's tape just dropped.

863
01:00:58,208 --> 01:01:00,208
[tense pulsing music playing]

864
01:01:02,041 --> 01:01:05,333
[Beck] We have confirmation Carter's
been talking to someone on the outside.

865
01:01:05,833 --> 01:01:06,833
What?

866
01:01:06,916 --> 01:01:08,166
I'm so sorry.

867
01:01:09,000 --> 01:01:11,000
[tense pulsing music building]

868
01:01:18,333 --> 01:01:21,708
[through headphones] <i>♪ I love you</i>
<i>So what am I so afraid of? ♪</i>

869
01:01:21,791 --> 01:01:24,166
<i>♪ I'm afraid that I'm not sure of ♪</i>

870
01:01:24,250 --> 01:01:25,875
<i>♪ A love there is no cure… ♪</i>

871
01:01:25,958 --> 01:01:28,500
No. Jake was made to say those things.

872
01:01:28,583 --> 01:01:30,583
[sobbing quietly]

873
01:01:32,666 --> 01:01:35,000
He's alive.
That's the most important thing.

874
01:01:35,083 --> 01:01:36,166
Yeah, but…

875
01:01:38,458 --> 01:01:39,708
for how long?

876
01:01:41,041 --> 01:01:43,125
[Pete] Come on.
Let me take you home. Come on.

877
01:01:44,291 --> 01:01:45,166
Hmm?

878
01:01:47,875 --> 01:01:49,208
[sniffles] Okay.

879
01:01:55,500 --> 01:01:57,291
[microwave beeps]

880
01:01:57,375 --> 01:01:58,583
[door opens]

881
01:01:58,666 --> 01:01:59,958
[Tom] What's with that crack?

882
01:02:02,000 --> 01:02:06,166
Keeps opening up, no matter how many times
I try to plaster the damn thing.

883
01:02:06,250 --> 01:02:07,166
[Tom] Uh-huh.

884
01:02:18,333 --> 01:02:19,750
Thank you. Um…

885
01:02:23,208 --> 01:02:26,750
-Tom, we spoke to Frank Carter.
-You did?

886
01:02:26,833 --> 01:02:30,333
[Pete] He's had contact with someone
on the outside through another inmate.

887
01:02:30,416 --> 01:02:32,750
Someone named Victor Tyler.
He's a pedophile.

888
01:02:32,833 --> 01:02:35,791
And there was a burner phone found
in Tyler's cell.

889
01:02:35,875 --> 01:02:37,208
Forensics is on that now.

890
01:02:37,291 --> 01:02:38,291
Pedophile?

891
01:02:40,708 --> 01:02:43,166
Jesus fucking Christ.

892
01:02:47,125 --> 01:02:48,083
What are you doing?

893
01:02:49,750 --> 01:02:51,083
That's not gonna help.

894
01:02:52,291 --> 01:02:53,875
There's no booze in this house.

895
01:02:57,250 --> 01:02:58,333
Okay.

896
01:03:03,083 --> 01:03:04,458
I know. I know. I know.

897
01:03:04,541 --> 01:03:06,625
It's unbearable, I know.

898
01:03:06,708 --> 01:03:10,291
Jake's gonna come home,
but it has to be to a safe home.

899
01:03:10,375 --> 01:03:13,083
And his dad has to be all right.

900
01:03:13,750 --> 01:03:15,375
[Tom] I was drinking the night…

901
01:03:16,416 --> 01:03:17,333
We had an argument.

902
01:03:17,416 --> 01:03:20,166
"We had an argument."
I fucking yelled at him.

903
01:03:20,875 --> 01:03:26,708
To walk out that door into the dark,
he had to feel so alone.

904
01:03:26,791 --> 01:03:28,833
[somber music playing]

905
01:03:30,083 --> 01:03:33,500
When Rebecca died,
he found her at the bottom of the stairs,

906
01:03:33,583 --> 01:03:36,291
and now he can't even
climb a fucking flight of stairs.

907
01:03:38,375 --> 01:03:41,416
I mean, I thought it would be
a good change moving here.

908
01:03:42,500 --> 01:03:44,166
He held on to his mom's stuff.

909
01:03:46,458 --> 01:03:49,833
Photos and notes and old diaries and…

910
01:03:51,791 --> 01:03:53,500
In this satchel.

911
01:03:53,583 --> 01:03:56,750
He called it his Packet of Special Things.

912
01:03:58,958 --> 01:04:00,541
Hey, when you left us,

913
01:04:01,750 --> 01:04:03,666
didn't you want to reach out?

914
01:04:03,750 --> 01:04:06,041
Of course I… I… I… [sighs]

915
01:04:06,125 --> 01:04:07,125
Every day.

916
01:04:07,875 --> 01:04:10,583
Why didn't you? Weren't you curious?

917
01:04:14,083 --> 01:04:17,500
You know, she never spoke badly
about you, not once, Mom.

918
01:04:17,583 --> 01:04:19,166
Even after everything.

919
01:04:24,041 --> 01:04:27,041
There were times before you guys
moved away where your mother would say,

920
01:04:27,125 --> 01:04:30,833
"Look, you can see him,
but you can't be drinking."

921
01:04:31,666 --> 01:04:34,875
And so I would see you,
and I'd read you stories

922
01:04:34,958 --> 01:04:36,916
when you were about to go to sleep.

923
01:04:37,000 --> 01:04:40,333
And I would tell you how much I love you,
kiss you on the forehead.

924
01:04:41,625 --> 01:04:43,000
And she gave me that.

925
01:04:48,208 --> 01:04:49,541
Mr. Night?

926
01:04:51,041 --> 01:04:52,375
You're Mr. Night?

927
01:04:55,916 --> 01:04:56,875
You?

928
01:04:57,833 --> 01:04:59,250
That was you?

929
01:05:09,291 --> 01:05:11,291
[Pete] There's an extra bed
if you wanna stay.

930
01:05:12,583 --> 01:05:13,625
It's all made up.

931
01:05:18,250 --> 01:05:19,125
[rattling]

932
01:05:19,208 --> 01:05:23,666
[dog barking]

933
01:06:00,166 --> 01:06:02,166
[ominous music playing]

934
01:06:49,166 --> 01:06:50,833
They were pen pals.

935
01:06:50,916 --> 01:06:52,333
Did you know about this?

936
01:06:53,583 --> 01:06:56,750
What the fuck else is my dad not sharing?

937
01:06:56,833 --> 01:06:58,375
This isn't the place.

938
01:06:58,958 --> 01:06:59,833
What?

939
01:07:02,541 --> 01:07:05,333
Oh, is… is God listening to us right now?

940
01:07:05,416 --> 01:07:06,750
[cell phone buzzing]

941
01:07:06,833 --> 01:07:09,291
Maybe that's him, with some leads.

942
01:07:12,125 --> 01:07:14,166
[Beck] Tell me we have a search warrant.

943
01:07:16,083 --> 01:07:17,791
[Beck talking quietly on phone]

944
01:07:25,166 --> 01:07:28,083
[Beck continues talking quietly]

945
01:08:19,166 --> 01:08:21,333
Where the fuck is this guy going?

946
01:08:48,333 --> 01:08:50,375
Anything else you're not telling us?

947
01:08:50,458 --> 01:08:55,500
Carter sent those letters to hurt my son,
but I kept them secret to deny him that.

948
01:08:55,583 --> 01:08:58,750
You still kept them.
Norman Collins would be impressed.

949
01:09:03,666 --> 01:09:05,625
Fucking prick.

950
01:09:07,958 --> 01:09:09,000
You…

951
01:09:09,083 --> 01:09:10,541
[tires squeal]

952
01:09:11,333 --> 01:09:14,333
-[dramatic music playing]
-[kids clamoring]

953
01:09:16,208 --> 01:09:18,416
-[Tom] Where is he?
-[Collins] What are you doing? My God!

954
01:09:18,500 --> 01:09:20,000
Motherfucker! Where is he?

955
01:09:20,083 --> 01:09:21,333
Where's my boy?

956
01:09:21,416 --> 01:09:22,708
Oh God!

957
01:09:22,791 --> 01:09:25,208
-[Tom grunts]
-[Collins whimpers]

958
01:09:25,291 --> 01:09:26,958
Help! Help!

959
01:09:27,041 --> 01:09:28,125
-Where is he?
-Help!

960
01:09:28,208 --> 01:09:30,500
-[man] Hey! Come on!
-No!

961
01:09:31,166 --> 01:09:34,083
That guy kidnapped my son!
You're letting him get away!

962
01:09:34,166 --> 01:09:35,625
That's the Whisper Man!

963
01:09:35,708 --> 01:09:37,541
That's the Whisper Man!

964
01:09:37,625 --> 01:09:39,666
Back inside! Let's go! Now!

965
01:09:39,750 --> 01:09:41,041
[all clamoring]

966
01:09:41,625 --> 01:09:42,541
[teacher] Back inside!

967
01:09:42,625 --> 01:09:43,791
That's the Whisper Man!

968
01:09:43,875 --> 01:09:47,208
[Beck] What were you doing
in the basement of 13 Garholt Street?

969
01:09:47,958 --> 01:09:50,333
Uh, I don't know that address.

970
01:09:50,416 --> 01:09:52,458
-[Dyson] Norman, stop bullshitting us.
-[Beck scoffs]

971
01:09:52,541 --> 01:09:54,083
[Dyson] The owner saw you.

972
01:09:55,541 --> 01:09:57,541
If you're referring
to the man who just attacked me,

973
01:09:57,625 --> 01:09:59,125
I've never seen him before in my life.

974
01:09:59,208 --> 01:10:02,916
[Beck] My guys just searched your place.
This is underlined. So are the others.

975
01:10:05,291 --> 01:10:06,666
[Collins] I like his stories.

976
01:10:06,750 --> 01:10:08,333
[Dyson] What do you like about them?

977
01:10:08,875 --> 01:10:12,041
Well, he's got this dark mind,

978
01:10:12,125 --> 01:10:13,666
sort of like his daddy's.

979
01:10:14,166 --> 01:10:16,208
[Beck] We talked to Victor Tyler.

980
01:10:16,291 --> 01:10:20,166
We know that you used him
to pass on a private note to Frank Carter

981
01:10:20,250 --> 01:10:23,458
and a burner phone so he could communicate
with someone on the outside.

982
01:10:23,541 --> 01:10:27,666
And now children are disappearing
and turning up dead.

983
01:10:28,166 --> 01:10:29,958
I don't know, but it all points to you.

984
01:10:30,041 --> 01:10:32,916
-No. No, no, no, no, no.
-[Beck] Then what?

985
01:10:34,000 --> 01:10:35,916
Were you just getting his autograph?

986
01:10:36,708 --> 01:10:39,291
Another souvenir
for your sicko collection?

987
01:10:42,666 --> 01:10:44,625
I wouldn't hurt those kids, any kids.

988
01:10:46,458 --> 01:10:49,208
-Where the fuck is he going?
-[Pete] There's not enough to hold him.

989
01:10:49,291 --> 01:10:51,791
[Beck] He's accounted for both nights
the boys were kidnapped.

990
01:10:51,875 --> 01:10:54,208
In Jake's case,
that man was in another state.

991
01:10:54,291 --> 01:10:56,750
-So he couldn't have taken them.
-Not by himself.

992
01:10:56,833 --> 01:10:59,583
Collins wanted to press assault charges.
Still might.

993
01:10:59,666 --> 01:11:01,083
I hurt him? Are you kidding?

994
01:11:01,166 --> 01:11:03,250
Garretton PD will
only let you walk out of here tonight

995
01:11:03,333 --> 01:11:06,500
if you go home with your father here
and promise not to do anything stupid.

996
01:11:06,583 --> 01:11:07,750
[Tom] This man

997
01:11:08,375 --> 01:11:10,750
knows who has my boy.

998
01:11:17,916 --> 01:11:20,041
Please don't leave me.

999
01:11:27,875 --> 01:11:29,916
I was just trying to protect you.

1000
01:11:33,000 --> 01:11:34,375
Yeah, well…

1001
01:11:36,541 --> 01:11:41,333
Maybe that's the original sin
of… fathers everywhere.

1002
01:11:44,708 --> 01:11:45,750
We can't.

1003
01:11:55,875 --> 01:11:57,916
I'll be right back. [sighs]

1004
01:12:06,500 --> 01:12:07,583
[sighs]

1005
01:12:21,750 --> 01:12:24,000
[liquid pouring]

1006
01:12:32,583 --> 01:12:34,166
[dogs barking]

1007
01:12:42,250 --> 01:12:45,875
What was Norman doing in the basement?

1008
01:12:51,875 --> 01:12:54,666
If it really wasn't for Jake,
what was he looking for?

1009
01:13:39,250 --> 01:13:40,208
Dad.

1010
01:14:09,791 --> 01:14:12,791
[mysterious music playing]

1011
01:14:20,833 --> 01:14:22,833
[music building]

1012
01:14:43,208 --> 01:14:44,625
Boy in the floor.

1013
01:14:52,166 --> 01:14:54,375
[line ringing]

1014
01:14:54,458 --> 01:14:55,291
<i>Beck here.</i>

1015
01:14:55,375 --> 01:14:58,875
Yeah, we're at Garholt Street.
We just found Tony Smith.

1016
01:15:17,875 --> 01:15:19,166
Thirty years.

1017
01:15:20,541 --> 01:15:21,458
Collins knew.

1018
01:15:21,541 --> 01:15:23,875
What are we doing sitting here?

1019
01:15:34,125 --> 01:15:36,250
Hey, we got another body over here.

1020
01:15:36,333 --> 01:15:38,333
[dramatic music playing]

1021
01:15:48,041 --> 01:15:50,458
Some kind of blunt instrument.

1022
01:15:55,000 --> 01:15:56,041
[music fades]

1023
01:15:56,125 --> 01:15:59,083
["The Mikado: Behold
The Lord High Executioner" playing inside]

1024
01:15:59,166 --> 01:16:01,875
You better have
a very good excuse for harassing…

1025
01:16:01,958 --> 01:16:02,958
Hey! Hey!

1026
01:16:03,041 --> 01:16:05,958
We found Tony Smith's remains
on the Garholt property this morning.

1027
01:16:06,041 --> 01:16:07,291
[Pete] And another body.

1028
01:16:08,458 --> 01:16:09,416
[Beck] Provenance.

1029
01:16:09,500 --> 01:16:12,583
That's what you collectors call
where a thing comes from, right?

1030
01:16:13,791 --> 01:16:15,333
What's the provenance behind this?

1031
01:16:15,416 --> 01:16:18,166
Um, that was, uh, acquired off-market.

1032
01:16:18,250 --> 01:16:20,125
All aboveboard though, right?

1033
01:16:22,708 --> 01:16:24,625
Dominic Barnett. That name ring a bell?

1034
01:16:24,708 --> 01:16:27,000
He was found stuffed
in the wall of the basement.

1035
01:16:27,083 --> 01:16:28,916
His skull bashed in.

1036
01:16:31,125 --> 01:16:33,333
I don't know.
DNA will tell us if it's a match.

1037
01:16:33,416 --> 01:16:36,625
["Behold The Lord High Executioner"
continues playing over speakers]

1038
01:16:38,083 --> 01:16:39,791
Um, I want a lawyer.

1039
01:16:39,875 --> 01:16:42,291
You wanted in this game? You're in it.

1040
01:16:43,291 --> 01:16:45,291
I didn't hurt any children.

1041
01:16:45,375 --> 01:16:49,375
[sirens wailing]

1042
01:16:49,458 --> 01:16:50,708
Okay.

1043
01:16:50,791 --> 01:16:53,875
I paid Frank Carter for access.

1044
01:16:53,958 --> 01:16:57,166
Access? Access to who? Tony Smith?

1045
01:16:57,250 --> 01:16:59,791
-Maybe grab something for your collection?
-Okay. Yes.

1046
01:16:59,875 --> 01:17:01,625
So he pointed you to Dominic Barnett?

1047
01:17:01,708 --> 01:17:04,916
Yeah. Um, they… they were friends
back in the day.

1048
01:17:05,000 --> 01:17:07,125
Friends? They weren't friends.
They were accomplices.

1049
01:17:07,208 --> 01:17:09,750
What happened between you and Dominic
when you got to the house?

1050
01:17:09,833 --> 01:17:11,791
-He, um…
-[Pete] What happened?

1051
01:17:11,875 --> 01:17:14,500
He said, uh… He…

1052
01:17:14,583 --> 01:17:15,833
[breathing unsteadily]

1053
01:17:15,916 --> 01:17:16,916
[Pete] What happened?

1054
01:17:17,625 --> 01:17:21,250
In the basement,
he made me feel very small,

1055
01:17:21,333 --> 01:17:25,000
saying that I was a tourist
and that I was a Peeping Tom.

1056
01:17:25,083 --> 01:17:27,166
That I could jerk off but never fuck.

1057
01:17:27,250 --> 01:17:28,208
So you killed him?

1058
01:17:28,291 --> 01:17:31,416
[Pete] You killed him, didn't you?
And that I don't care about.

1059
01:17:31,500 --> 01:17:33,958
All I care about is
finding Jake Kennedy alive.

1060
01:17:34,833 --> 01:17:36,125
Do you understand?

1061
01:17:36,208 --> 01:17:37,583
[panting]

1062
01:17:37,666 --> 01:17:38,666
I can't…

1063
01:17:39,166 --> 01:17:40,875
-I can't go to prison.
-[Pete] You can't?

1064
01:17:41,458 --> 01:17:43,958
Well, that's too bad.
You're going to prison.

1065
01:17:44,541 --> 01:17:45,875
For a long time.

1066
01:17:45,958 --> 01:17:48,541
So you tell us everything
we need to know right now.

1067
01:17:49,541 --> 01:17:53,250
You just said you paid Frank Carter
for access to his last victim, Tony Smith,

1068
01:17:53,333 --> 01:17:55,750
who was never found.
Is that a fair statement?

1069
01:17:55,833 --> 01:17:57,666
-Yes.
-[Beck] Paid with what?

1070
01:17:57,750 --> 01:18:00,750
Carter's in prison for life.
No use for money.

1071
01:18:01,250 --> 01:18:03,791
No family anymore. What did you trade?

1072
01:18:05,833 --> 01:18:07,583
I connected him with someone.

1073
01:18:07,666 --> 01:18:10,458
Who? Norman, who did you connect him to?

1074
01:18:11,041 --> 01:18:12,125
[Beck] Who, Norman?

1075
01:18:14,333 --> 01:18:17,500
I was the only one who ever saw it.
In the eyes.

1076
01:18:18,000 --> 01:18:20,125
The eyes? Who are you talking about?

1077
01:18:20,208 --> 01:18:23,625
[whispers] I just thought that, you know,
they'd wanna get to know each other.

1078
01:18:23,708 --> 01:18:27,083
I never thought that…
that it was gonna start again.

1079
01:18:27,166 --> 01:18:30,333
Norman, we need a name. Who is it?

1080
01:18:31,416 --> 01:18:32,750
[Beck] The eyes.

1081
01:18:32,833 --> 01:18:34,833
The eyes. Who are you talking about?

1082
01:18:41,791 --> 01:18:43,375
[Beck screams, pants]

1083
01:18:43,916 --> 01:18:45,166
[Beck yelps]

1084
01:18:46,375 --> 01:18:47,208
We need a bus!

1085
01:18:47,291 --> 01:18:50,541
-Help! We need an ambulance!
-Where's Jake? Tell me, where's Jake?

1086
01:18:50,625 --> 01:18:53,166
That's the one thing you can do.
Tell me, where's Jake, please?

1087
01:18:53,250 --> 01:18:55,458
Where is Jake? Where's Jake?

1088
01:18:55,541 --> 01:18:57,833
-[man] Sir!
-[Pete] Just tell me where he is, please.

1089
01:18:57,916 --> 01:18:59,083
[officer] Please stand back!

1090
01:18:59,791 --> 01:19:01,041
Come on.

1091
01:19:01,125 --> 01:19:02,250
Stay with me.

1092
01:19:02,333 --> 01:19:05,833
[ominous music playing]

1093
01:19:28,416 --> 01:19:29,625
[music fades]

1094
01:19:29,708 --> 01:19:33,250
Tom was right. We should have beat
whatever the hell we needed out of him.

1095
01:19:33,333 --> 01:19:35,708
Norman said that he thought
Frank Carter would be interested

1096
01:19:35,791 --> 01:19:37,750
in getting to know this person. Why?

1097
01:19:37,833 --> 01:19:41,000
Why invest in someone
he'll never know, never meet?

1098
01:19:41,083 --> 01:19:42,208
Makes no sense.

1099
01:19:42,958 --> 01:19:45,541
Who is more important to Frank Carter
than you?

1100
01:19:49,208 --> 01:19:51,208
[indistinct background chatter]

1101
01:19:54,083 --> 01:19:57,375
What did Carter say to us
when we were leaving?

1102
01:19:57,875 --> 01:19:59,291
[Beck] The sixth victim?

1103
01:20:00,250 --> 01:20:01,125
[Pete] No.

1104
01:20:02,666 --> 01:20:04,625
About my son's novels.

1105
01:20:06,500 --> 01:20:08,041
He's trying to be you.

1106
01:20:12,291 --> 01:20:14,500
Pull up the interview
with Frank Carter's wife.

1107
01:20:19,041 --> 01:20:21,083
That's the one. Play it.

1108
01:20:22,791 --> 01:20:24,583
<i>I was afraid for my son.</i>

1109
01:20:25,791 --> 01:20:28,583
[Pete on video] <i>You don't have</i>
<i>to be afraid anymore, Mrs. Carter.</i>

1110
01:20:28,666 --> 01:20:29,875
<i>You're safe now.</i>

1111
01:20:31,041 --> 01:20:34,833
<i>There's another boy still missing, though,</i>
<i>and he might still be alive.</i>

1112
01:20:35,333 --> 01:20:36,916
<i>You can help us find him.</i>

1113
01:20:37,000 --> 01:20:38,666
<i>He's somebody's son too.</i>

1114
01:20:39,500 --> 01:20:41,250
<i>I've told you everything I know.</i>

1115
01:20:52,833 --> 01:20:55,708
[Beck] "When we're denied
our father's love,

1116
01:20:55,791 --> 01:20:57,375
we mythologize him."

1117
01:20:59,208 --> 01:21:00,166
It's him.

1118
01:21:06,041 --> 01:21:08,875
Do you ever feel like a boy in the floor,

1119
01:21:10,500 --> 01:21:12,500
underneath everyone's feet,

1120
01:21:13,458 --> 01:21:15,250
who no one knows is there?

1121
01:21:16,458 --> 01:21:17,500
I do.

1122
01:21:19,083 --> 01:21:22,750
Did the boy in the floor
go to sleep forever?

1123
01:21:26,041 --> 01:21:27,125
He did.

1124
01:21:32,791 --> 01:21:36,000
Are you going to make me
go to sleep forever?

1125
01:21:37,041 --> 01:21:39,041
I'm going to bring you home.

1126
01:21:45,125 --> 01:21:47,875
[Beck] <i>After Carter's conviction,</i>
<i>the family moved out west</i>

1127
01:21:47,958 --> 01:21:49,208
and assumed new identities.

1128
01:21:49,291 --> 01:21:52,000
We have no name, no ID.

1129
01:21:52,083 --> 01:21:55,791
We're negotiating with the FBI
to release whatever records they do have

1130
01:21:55,875 --> 01:21:59,000
because, technically, Francis Jr.
is still under their protection.

1131
01:21:59,083 --> 01:22:02,666
In the meantime, we need to canvas
anyone and everyone

1132
01:22:02,750 --> 01:22:04,833
in Hillcrest
and the surrounding neighborhoods.

1133
01:22:04,916 --> 01:22:07,916
If Francis Jr. is here,
someone knows where to find him.

1134
01:22:08,000 --> 01:22:09,125
Let's go.

1135
01:22:16,875 --> 01:22:18,833
[sirens wailing]

1136
01:22:18,916 --> 01:22:20,250
[over radio] <i>All units be advised.</i>

1137
01:22:20,333 --> 01:22:23,125
<i>The suspect has been identified</i>
<i>as Francis Carter, Jr.,</i>

1138
01:22:23,208 --> 01:22:24,958
<i>residing in Garretton.</i>

1139
01:22:25,041 --> 01:22:29,208
<i>We'll conduct a block-by-block canvas</i>
<i>in an attempt to locate the suspect.</i>

1140
01:22:29,291 --> 01:22:30,166
<i>Car 431.</i>

1141
01:22:30,875 --> 01:22:33,666
<i>Cover the 400 block of Lafayette,</i>
<i>heading east.</i>

1142
01:22:34,250 --> 01:22:38,750
<i>Car 595. Cover Maple Avenue</i>
<i>on the 200 block, heading south.</i>

1143
01:22:53,500 --> 01:22:55,000
[door buzzing]

1144
01:23:15,666 --> 01:23:17,291
[door locking]

1145
01:23:19,291 --> 01:23:21,083
How's your grandson, Pete?

1146
01:23:22,625 --> 01:23:25,416
Good afternoon.
Detective Amanda Beck, Garretton PD.

1147
01:23:25,500 --> 01:23:27,333
I'm looking for Richard Sharmatz.

1148
01:23:28,875 --> 01:23:34,041
Ah, Dr. Sharmatz, uh, passed away
about a year ago.

1149
01:23:34,125 --> 01:23:35,541
Oh, his name's still on the title.

1150
01:23:35,625 --> 01:23:37,916
His family rents the house to me.

1151
01:23:38,000 --> 01:23:40,125
He was a mentor of… of mine.

1152
01:23:40,208 --> 01:23:42,208
-[Beck] Oh.
-I'm George Carringdon.

1153
01:23:42,291 --> 01:23:43,125
-Hi.
-Hi.

1154
01:23:43,208 --> 01:23:45,166
You a child psychologist as well?

1155
01:23:45,666 --> 01:23:47,000
Teaching assistant.

1156
01:23:47,083 --> 01:23:48,000
Where?

1157
01:23:48,916 --> 01:23:50,083
-Rose Terrace.
-[Beck] Huh.

1158
01:23:50,750 --> 01:23:53,250
Do you know a Jake Kennedy?
He was a student there.

1159
01:23:54,875 --> 01:23:57,500
Not until they announced what happened.

1160
01:23:58,041 --> 01:24:01,625
I… I probably saw him
running through the halls out at recess,

1161
01:24:01,708 --> 01:24:04,541
but, um, I work with
the special needs kids.

1162
01:24:04,625 --> 01:24:06,833
-Oh.
-So I wouldn't have known him by name.

1163
01:24:08,000 --> 01:24:09,083
Do you want to come in?

1164
01:24:09,583 --> 01:24:10,625
[door closes]

1165
01:24:15,541 --> 01:24:17,958
Did you, by any chance,
know the Carter family back in the day?

1166
01:24:18,041 --> 01:24:20,583
Frank and Jane, their son Francis Jr.

1167
01:24:20,666 --> 01:24:21,625
Of them.

1168
01:24:22,125 --> 01:24:25,958
My parents tried to keep me away
from all that stuff. Didn't work.

1169
01:24:26,041 --> 01:24:28,208
We know you've been in communication
with your son,

1170
01:24:28,291 --> 01:24:29,666
prodding him with these killings.

1171
01:24:30,250 --> 01:24:33,625
Boy left home, and now he's back.

1172
01:24:33,708 --> 01:24:34,791
Got lost.

1173
01:24:35,958 --> 01:24:37,208
He's back home now.

1174
01:24:37,708 --> 01:24:38,833
That surprise you?

1175
01:24:38,916 --> 01:24:40,083
Not really, no.

1176
01:24:40,166 --> 01:24:43,916
I mean, Francis has always been weak.
Look how he…

1177
01:24:44,666 --> 01:24:46,583
how he fucked up the first try.

1178
01:24:48,041 --> 01:24:49,708
[Beck] I guess it's hard with kids.

1179
01:24:49,791 --> 01:24:52,083
Well, scary stories are like water.

1180
01:24:54,583 --> 01:24:56,833
They always find their way
through the cracks.

1181
01:24:56,916 --> 01:25:01,500
I remember growing up in Fair Lawn.
There was this rhyme.

1182
01:25:02,875 --> 01:25:04,666
<i>If you leave a door half open</i>

1183
01:25:04,750 --> 01:25:06,708
<i>Soon you'll hear the whisper spoken</i>

1184
01:25:06,791 --> 01:25:09,583
-[both] <i>If your window's…</i>
-[George] <i>…left unlatched</i>

1185
01:25:09,666 --> 01:25:11,541
<i>You'll hear him tapping at the glass</i>

1186
01:25:12,041 --> 01:25:14,458
<i>-If you're lonely…</i>
-[both] <i>…sad, or blue…</i>

1187
01:25:15,083 --> 01:25:16,375
[clock ticking]

1188
01:25:16,458 --> 01:25:18,500
<i>The Whisper Man will come for you</i>

1189
01:25:25,333 --> 01:25:27,666
Been a long time
since I've heard that one.

1190
01:25:29,041 --> 01:25:33,041
[kettle whistling]

1191
01:25:33,125 --> 01:25:35,083
I was making tea. You want a cup?

1192
01:25:40,458 --> 01:25:42,833
I get now
why you always covered their faces.

1193
01:25:42,916 --> 01:25:46,125
I thought it was 'cause you couldn't look
at 'em or didn't want them looking at you.

1194
01:25:46,208 --> 01:25:48,291
Nah, I could look at their faces
just fine.

1195
01:25:48,375 --> 01:25:49,791
[Pete] Oh, that's bullshit. Come on.

1196
01:25:49,875 --> 01:25:51,875
You know there was someone
you were imagining

1197
01:25:51,958 --> 01:25:55,041
you wanted to get a hold of
but you couldn't really get your hands on.

1198
01:25:56,791 --> 01:25:58,833
It was too painful, too messy,

1199
01:25:58,916 --> 01:26:00,166
too close to home.

1200
01:26:00,250 --> 01:26:03,416
Well… home is where the heart is, Pete.

1201
01:26:04,583 --> 01:26:09,000
[George] Is there some sort of connection
between Frank Carter and Dr. Sharmatz?

1202
01:26:10,000 --> 01:26:14,041
He counseled Carter's son,
according to records.

1203
01:26:14,125 --> 01:26:16,416
[ominous music playing]

1204
01:26:16,500 --> 01:26:18,833
[George] Police must be stretched
pretty thin.

1205
01:26:20,083 --> 01:26:21,958
No partner, I see.

1206
01:26:23,541 --> 01:26:25,708
Everybody has their ground to cover.

1207
01:26:26,375 --> 01:26:30,916
I know the parents will be relieved
that you're chasing down some leads.

1208
01:26:31,541 --> 01:26:34,166
Yeah. Kids, too, I'm guessing.

1209
01:26:34,666 --> 01:26:37,500
Francis is learning his own lessons
right now.

1210
01:26:38,000 --> 01:26:40,333
Yeah. Like you did with your father?

1211
01:26:41,875 --> 01:26:43,333
The way he taught you.

1212
01:26:43,416 --> 01:26:45,750
Whispering to you in bed
while he was fucking you up the ass?

1213
01:26:45,833 --> 01:26:47,375
[laughs] You better shut up.

1214
01:26:47,458 --> 01:26:49,458
How'd you handle those situations, Frank?

1215
01:26:49,541 --> 01:26:52,125
Did you wish you were somewhere
like the kids you took did too?

1216
01:26:52,208 --> 01:26:53,375
-Fuck you.
-[Pete] Ah.

1217
01:26:53,458 --> 01:26:55,625
Your father whet his appetite
with his own son.

1218
01:26:55,708 --> 01:26:58,166
-[Carter] Fuck you.
-But you, you were the weak one.

1219
01:27:01,875 --> 01:27:04,333
I actually respect you, Frank.
You know that?

1220
01:27:04,416 --> 01:27:08,291
You tried to stop yourself from doing
what you really wanted to do to your boy.

1221
01:27:08,791 --> 01:27:09,791
Yeah.

1222
01:27:10,958 --> 01:27:12,625
So you preyed on others.

1223
01:27:12,708 --> 01:27:15,500
When we catch your son,
and we're gonna catch him very soon…

1224
01:27:15,583 --> 01:27:18,125
-Yeah?
-You're never gonna hear from him again.

1225
01:27:18,208 --> 01:27:20,416
Oh, really? So…

1226
01:27:20,500 --> 01:27:22,500
So there's another possibility.

1227
01:27:23,666 --> 01:27:24,625
Jake.

1228
01:27:25,416 --> 01:27:26,875
You can tell me where he is.

1229
01:27:26,958 --> 01:27:27,791
[laughs softly]

1230
01:27:30,750 --> 01:27:32,541
Why would I do that before the deed?

1231
01:27:32,625 --> 01:27:35,500
Because the Whisper Man,
the real one, isn't done yet.

1232
01:27:36,083 --> 01:27:38,916
Because there's only one child
in this whole world

1233
01:27:39,000 --> 01:27:41,458
that he truly, really wants.

1234
01:27:41,958 --> 01:27:43,750
And I can deliver him to you.

1235
01:27:45,250 --> 01:27:46,500
[Carter] My son?

1236
01:27:51,250 --> 01:27:52,208
Here?

1237
01:27:52,291 --> 01:27:55,458
A father does what needs to be done.
Wouldn't you agree?

1238
01:27:59,833 --> 01:28:02,291
[Beck] If you think of anyone
that might know the Carter family,

1239
01:28:02,375 --> 01:28:06,083
especially Francis Jr.,
please have them call me, okay?

1240
01:28:09,583 --> 01:28:11,166
-Of course.
-[cell phone chimes]

1241
01:28:12,041 --> 01:28:14,041
[clock ticking]

1242
01:28:20,708 --> 01:28:22,500
-[George grunts]
-[Beck] Oh fuck!

1243
01:28:22,583 --> 01:28:24,833
[Beck panting]

1244
01:28:24,916 --> 01:28:27,500
[running footsteps]

1245
01:28:30,541 --> 01:28:34,458
This is Beck. I need backup.
59 Hellerman Street. I found our suspect.

1246
01:28:34,541 --> 01:28:36,375
-[man] <i>Copy that.</i>
-[thud]

1247
01:28:36,958 --> 01:28:38,291
Jake Kennedy?

1248
01:28:39,166 --> 01:28:40,500
This is the police.

1249
01:28:40,583 --> 01:28:42,583
[tense music playing]

1250
01:29:47,083 --> 01:29:49,083
[Beck panting]

1251
01:30:13,583 --> 01:30:15,458
[air hisses]

1252
01:30:26,333 --> 01:30:27,666
Scream.

1253
01:30:31,500 --> 01:30:34,208
[Jake yelling] Help!

1254
01:30:34,291 --> 01:30:36,291
[pulsing tense music building]

1255
01:30:42,625 --> 01:30:45,125
-[George grunts]
-[Beck screams]

1256
01:30:46,250 --> 01:30:47,333
[George grunts]

1257
01:30:47,416 --> 01:30:48,250
[Beck groans]

1258
01:30:55,291 --> 01:30:56,125
[door unlocks]

1259
01:30:56,958 --> 01:30:59,416
[yelling] Get up! Come on!

1260
01:31:11,916 --> 01:31:13,083
-[Beck grunts]
-[George yells]

1261
01:31:17,333 --> 01:31:19,625
[Jake whimpering]

1262
01:31:21,333 --> 01:31:23,083
[panting] Run!

1263
01:31:23,166 --> 01:31:25,708
[whimpering]

1264
01:31:25,791 --> 01:31:26,750
[Beck] Run!

1265
01:31:32,000 --> 01:31:33,333
[George groans]

1266
01:31:38,708 --> 01:31:40,041
Help!

1267
01:31:40,125 --> 01:31:41,166
Stop!

1268
01:31:42,208 --> 01:31:44,875
Help! Help!

1269
01:31:52,416 --> 01:31:53,708
[engine turns over]

1270
01:31:53,791 --> 01:31:55,250
[car pulls away]

1271
01:32:07,458 --> 01:32:11,041
[buzzing]

1272
01:32:11,125 --> 01:32:14,750
[sirens wailing]

1273
01:32:15,458 --> 01:32:17,250
<i>Detective Beck. Leave a message.</i>

1274
01:32:17,333 --> 01:32:19,833
Beck. Yeah. It's me.

1275
01:32:20,583 --> 01:32:23,083
I spoke to Carter.
They have a plan for Jake.

1276
01:32:23,166 --> 01:32:25,166
[unsettling music playing]

1277
01:32:34,625 --> 01:32:36,000
[tapping on phone]

1278
01:32:36,083 --> 01:32:37,666
[line ringing]

1279
01:32:39,041 --> 01:32:41,166
[operator] <i>Garretton Police.</i>
<i>What's your emergency?</i>

1280
01:32:41,250 --> 01:32:43,291
I just saw the missing boy, Jake Kennedy.

1281
01:32:43,375 --> 01:32:46,083
He was with a man,
Route 23, south of Sussex.

1282
01:32:46,166 --> 01:32:48,583
<i>Dispatch 10-17. We have units en route.</i>

1283
01:32:48,666 --> 01:32:51,333
<i>Can I please have your name</i>
<i>and a callback number?</i>

1284
01:32:59,333 --> 01:33:02,958
[siren wailing]

1285
01:33:16,750 --> 01:33:18,666
[Jake panting]

1286
01:33:20,083 --> 01:33:22,458
-[line ringing]
-What the hell?

1287
01:33:24,250 --> 01:33:27,125
[cell phone buzzing]

1288
01:33:27,208 --> 01:33:29,625
-[line continues ringing]
-Come on, Tom. Please pick up.

1289
01:33:39,000 --> 01:33:41,375
[line continues ringing]

1290
01:33:41,458 --> 01:33:42,333
[Tom] <i>Dad?</i>

1291
01:33:42,416 --> 01:33:44,416
[unsettling music continues playing]

1292
01:33:50,416 --> 01:33:51,583
[George] Sh.

1293
01:34:09,958 --> 01:34:11,958
[eerie music playing]

1294
01:34:24,208 --> 01:34:27,333
[alarm blaring]

1295
01:35:11,708 --> 01:35:13,416
-[Jake] I can't breathe!
-Jake!

1296
01:35:13,500 --> 01:35:14,541
[Jake] Dad, help!

1297
01:35:14,625 --> 01:35:17,875
[both grunt]

1298
01:35:17,958 --> 01:35:20,708
[Jake yelling]

1299
01:35:22,958 --> 01:35:24,958
[both grunting]

1300
01:35:27,208 --> 01:35:28,208
[Jake yells]

1301
01:35:30,083 --> 01:35:31,791
[Jake] Help!

1302
01:35:35,583 --> 01:35:36,416
[grunts]

1303
01:35:40,250 --> 01:35:42,833
-[Jake yelling]
-[Tom] Jake!

1304
01:35:44,208 --> 01:35:46,250
[Jake continues yelling]

1305
01:35:49,250 --> 01:35:50,666
[Jake panting]

1306
01:35:52,625 --> 01:35:54,250
Oh, Jake. It's okay.

1307
01:35:54,958 --> 01:35:56,041
[grunts]

1308
01:35:58,666 --> 01:36:00,416
Come on. Come on. Go.

1309
01:36:01,083 --> 01:36:03,791
[dramatic music playing]

1310
01:36:12,541 --> 01:36:14,083
-[Tom moans]
-Dad!

1311
01:36:19,500 --> 01:36:20,458
[Jake] Dad!

1312
01:36:21,291 --> 01:36:23,250
No!

1313
01:36:25,750 --> 01:36:26,916
Dad!

1314
01:36:27,000 --> 01:36:27,958
Dad!

1315
01:36:28,041 --> 01:36:29,333
Dad!

1316
01:36:29,958 --> 01:36:30,875
[Pete] Jake!

1317
01:36:30,958 --> 01:36:32,250
-[Jake] Dad!
-Jake!

1318
01:36:34,208 --> 01:36:36,291
Run! Run, Jake!

1319
01:36:36,791 --> 01:36:37,625
Run!

1320
01:36:39,791 --> 01:36:40,708
[groans]

1321
01:36:49,875 --> 01:36:52,166
Tommy, Tommy. Get Jake.

1322
01:36:52,250 --> 01:36:54,208
-Go get Jake.
-Dad! What?

1323
01:36:54,291 --> 01:36:56,166
-I love you.
-I love you.

1324
01:37:28,916 --> 01:37:30,250
[both grunt]

1325
01:37:43,500 --> 01:37:45,916
[both grunt]

1326
01:37:50,291 --> 01:37:51,833
Daddy!

1327
01:37:52,958 --> 01:37:54,500
Daddy!

1328
01:37:57,625 --> 01:37:58,625
[music calms]

1329
01:37:58,708 --> 01:38:01,750
[Jake panting]

1330
01:38:03,958 --> 01:38:05,000
[Tom] Jake.

1331
01:38:06,000 --> 01:38:09,125
Just stay. Stay there.

1332
01:38:10,250 --> 01:38:13,333
Jake, close your eyes.

1333
01:38:15,958 --> 01:38:17,250
[George] Agh!

1334
01:38:19,708 --> 01:38:21,000
[groaning]

1335
01:38:33,291 --> 01:38:36,291
[George breathing heavily]

1336
01:39:29,958 --> 01:39:32,583
[mysterious music playing]

1337
01:40:11,958 --> 01:40:15,958
[door unlocks, opens]

1338
01:40:16,041 --> 01:40:17,875
[man] Just make it quick, Carter.

1339
01:40:33,083 --> 01:40:34,666
Skin to skin,

1340
01:40:36,708 --> 01:40:38,666
like they said in the hospital,

1341
01:40:39,541 --> 01:40:41,583
to bond you to me.

1342
01:40:41,666 --> 01:40:43,666
[unsettling music playing]

1343
01:40:55,250 --> 01:40:56,791
[gasping]

1344
01:41:00,416 --> 01:41:02,416
[George choking]

1345
01:41:02,500 --> 01:41:04,500
[unsettling music building]

1346
01:41:27,541 --> 01:41:29,541
[music calms]

1347
01:41:45,958 --> 01:41:48,958
[solemn music playing]

1348
01:42:02,500 --> 01:42:04,500
[music fades]

1349
01:42:08,416 --> 01:42:10,958
What's Pearl Jam?

1350
01:42:11,041 --> 01:42:12,958
What? A band!

1351
01:42:13,041 --> 01:42:14,666
Clearly failed as a father.

1352
01:42:14,750 --> 01:42:16,875
It was our first concert, your mom and me.

1353
01:42:20,583 --> 01:42:21,583
She saved me.

1354
01:42:29,958 --> 01:42:30,958
Mommy?

1355
01:42:31,458 --> 01:42:32,375
Mm-hmm.

1356
01:42:35,083 --> 01:42:36,291
Yeah, me too.

1357
01:42:37,291 --> 01:42:39,291
[kids shouting outside]

1358
01:42:40,541 --> 01:42:42,208
Can I go play?

1359
01:42:43,916 --> 01:42:44,875
Yeah, dude.

1360
01:42:46,833 --> 01:42:47,916
Get out there.

1361
01:42:48,000 --> 01:42:49,583
-What are you doing in here?
-[chuckles]

1362
01:42:51,625 --> 01:42:52,708
[door opens]

1363
01:42:54,250 --> 01:42:55,375
[door closes]

1364
01:42:56,791 --> 01:42:57,958
[Jake] Hey, guys!

1365
01:42:58,041 --> 01:42:59,708
[kids continue shouting]

1366
01:43:29,625 --> 01:43:31,916
[gentle ethereal music playing]

1367
01:44:14,666 --> 01:44:16,916
[ethereal music continues]

1368
01:45:32,458 --> 01:45:33,958
[music fades]

1369
01:45:36,333 --> 01:45:38,333
[haunting music playing]

1370
01:49:03,333 --> 01:49:05,333
[somber music playing]

1371
01:51:00,916 --> 01:51:02,916
[music fades]